asr-002268
02:19:28.760 --> 02:19:29.204
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Good afternoon.

asr-002269
02:19:29.322 --> 02:19:32.101
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Commissioner, could you explain what the border,

asr-002270
02:19:32.188 --> 02:19:36.565
Rep. Allan U. Ty: border management information system, or BMIS, is?

asr-002271
02:19:39.278 --> 02:19:40.689
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Sir, good afternoon.

asr-002272
02:19:40.810 --> 02:19:50.143
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thank you very much, Congressman Ty, for giving us the opportunity to explain and to build trust with the Filipino people concerning this matter.

asr-002273
02:19:50.808 --> 02:19:57.279
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The large-scale border security system is needed at this point

asr-002274
02:19:58.670 --> 02:20:04.153
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: because this pertains to a technology-driven, AI-driven,

asr-002275
02:20:04.697 --> 02:20:08.608
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: biometric-driven kind of border control, Your Honor.

asr-002276
02:20:08.930 --> 02:20:14.574
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The concept really is to extend our borders beyond the actual physical border of the Philippines.

asr-002277
02:20:15.381 --> 02:20:26.468
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We plan to institute a system wherein even if a passenger is in another country and is not qualified to enter the Philippines,

asr-002278
02:20:26.468 --> 02:20:31.588
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: he will be prevented from doing so using this technology-driven system, Your Honor.

asr-002279
02:20:33.160 --> 02:20:34.705
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What is the total project?

asr-002280
02:20:34.741 --> 02:20:36.537
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What is the total project cost of BMIS?

asr-002281
02:20:37.345 --> 02:20:41.068
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The total project cost—this is a PPP project, Your Honor.

asr-002282
02:20:41.678 --> 02:20:51.118
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The total project cost for the first five years will be shouldered by the private proponent, amounting to about 10.7 billion, Your Honor.

asr-002283
02:20:51.423 --> 02:21:03.873
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But in the next 20 years, they will put in additional capital and maintenance expenses, amounting to about 52.5 billion, Your Honor.

asr-002284
02:21:03.873 --> 02:21:04.649
Rep. Allan U. Ty: How much is that?

asr-002285
02:21:04.665 --> 02:21:06.218
Rep. Allan U. Ty: How much is the national government share?

asr-002286
02:21:06.218 --> 02:21:14.380
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The government share would amount to, for passengers, the cost would be about $4, Your Honor.

asr-002287
02:21:14.380 --> 02:21:18.462
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: $3.80 will go to the private proponent and $0.20 will go to the Philippine government, Your Honor.

asr-002288
02:21:19.482 --> 02:21:24.219
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Is there no allocations made to BMIS by the national government?

asr-002289
02:21:26.114 --> 02:21:33.261
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: At this point, Your Honor, the intention really is to adopt a stepladder approach.

asr-002290
02:21:34.281 --> 02:21:44.572
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Any budget that has been allocated by government at this point, sad to say, in a way, is lacking.

asr-002291
02:21:45.512 --> 02:21:55.313
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So this PVP project will make up for any differences or any shortfalls that we might have as far as border control is concerned, Your Honor.

asr-002292
02:21:56.742 --> 02:22:03.555
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Based on your 2024 GAA, there's an allocation of four-point-something billion for BMIS.

asr-002293
02:22:04.734 --> 02:22:06.732
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Can you kindly confirm?

asr-002294
02:22:06.732 --> 02:22:16.700
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: For the year 2024, I think it was 1.9 billion, Your Honor, for the e-Gates project.

asr-002295
02:22:17.667 --> 02:22:23.118
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So there is a government fund used for the BMIS project?

asr-002296
02:22:23.118 --> 02:22:26.140
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's correct, Your Honor, for the E-Gates project.

asr-002297
02:22:26.140 --> 02:22:32.185
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Initially, it was funded at around 1.9 billion, but eventually it was reduced.

asr-002298
02:22:32.185 --> 02:22:35.208
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The winning bidder submitted a proposal.

asr-002299
02:22:35.208 --> 02:22:39.238
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Which was eventually accepted, which amounted to 1.5 billion.

asr-002300
02:22:39.238 --> 02:22:43.268
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But, Your Honor, this only pertains to the E-Gates project.

asr-002301
02:22:43.268 --> 02:22:50.320
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It does not pertain to any total border control system, which the private proponent is proposing, Your Honor.

