BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Consequently, the contract was awarded in December 2025.

asr-002356
02:26:16.654 --> 02:26:19.668
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Now, as the project is being implemented in phases,

asr-002357
02:26:19.668 --> 02:26:21.677
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: the delay in Phase 1 necessarily affected

asr-002358
02:26:21.677 --> 02:26:24.691
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: the procurement schedule of Phase 2.

asr-002359
02:26:24.691 --> 02:26:28.710
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: For Fiscal Year 2025, amounting to 1.3 billion.

asr-002360
02:26:28.710 --> 02:26:30.719
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And Phase 3, Fiscal Year 2026,

asr-002361
02:26:30.719 --> 02:26:33.733
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: amounting to 565 million.

asr-002362
02:26:33.733 --> 02:26:37.752
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The Bureau has since completed the required revisions

asr-002363
02:26:37.752 --> 02:26:39.761
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: revisions and is expediting, Your Honor,

asr-002364
02:26:39.761 --> 02:26:42.775
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: the remaining procurement activities.

asr-002365
02:26:42.775 --> 02:26:45.789
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And the Bureau assures that it will be able to award Phase 2

asr-002366
02:26:45.789 --> 02:26:49.807
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and other Fiscal Year 2025 and 2026 funded projects

asr-002367
02:26:49.807 --> 02:26:50.812
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: within the current year

asr-002368
02:26:50.812 --> 02:26:53.826
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and commits to fully implementing the modernization program

asr-002369
02:26:53.826 --> 02:26:55.835
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: as scheduled, Your Honor.

asr-002370
02:26:55.835 --> 02:26:58.163
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Last question, Cong. Allan.

asr-002371
02:26:58.163 --> 02:26:59.184
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I have...

asr-002372
02:27:00.205 --> 02:27:02.247
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I'll do my second round, Mr. Chairman.

asr-002373
02:27:02.247 --> 02:27:03.085
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Okay.

asr-002374
02:27:03.085 --> 02:27:04.762
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Yes, sir. Thank you.

asr-002375
02:27:08.240 --> 02:27:12.303
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line, from the majority,

asr-002376
02:27:12.303 --> 02:27:15.429
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Representative Solomon Chungalao.

asr-002377
02:27:15.439 --> 02:27:17.453
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Thank you, Chairman.

asr-002378
02:27:17.453 --> 02:27:21.482
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I just ask one question.

asr-002379
02:27:21.482 --> 02:27:23.496
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: My major question.

asr-002380
02:27:23.496 --> 02:27:25.510
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: One or two, perhaps.

asr-002381
02:27:25.510 --> 02:27:27.525
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Hypothetical.

asr-002382
02:27:27.525 --> 02:27:31.553
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: It pertains to the right of the government

asr-002383
02:27:31.553 --> 02:27:33.568
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: to expropriate private property

asr-002384
02:27:33.568 --> 02:27:35.582
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: for public use.

asr-002385
02:27:35.582 --> 02:27:38.603
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Now, if an agency exercises

asr-002386
02:27:38.603 --> 02:27:42.632
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: the power of expropriation,

asr-002387
02:27:42.632 --> 02:27:44.646
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: acquires private property

asr-002388
02:27:44.646 --> 02:27:46.661
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: for public use,

asr-002389
02:27:46.661 --> 02:27:48.675
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: but it's a private corporation

asr-002390
02:27:48.675 --> 02:27:51.696
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: pays the value,

asr-002391
02:27:51.696 --> 02:27:53.711
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: is there a proper exercise

asr-002392
02:27:53.711 --> 02:27:55.725
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: of the power of expropriation,

asr-002393
02:27:55.725 --> 02:28:03.349
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Secretary?

asr-002394
02:28:03.359 --> 02:28:06.512
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Elements for the proper exercise

asr-002395
02:28:06.512 --> 02:28:08.614
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: of expropriate...

asr-002396
02:28:08.614 --> 02:28:10.716
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: the right of eminent domain.

asr-002397
02:28:10.716 --> 02:28:12.818
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: One, public purpose.

asr-002398
02:28:12.818 --> 02:28:14.919
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Second, it's a...

asr-002399
02:28:14.919 --> 02:28:17.021
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: it's a...

asr-002400
02:28:17.021 --> 02:28:19.123
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: public purpose of the ano, no?

asr-002401
02:28:19.123 --> 02:28:22.276
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: And it would be utilizing public funds.

asr-002402
02:28:22.276 --> 02:28:24.378
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: But, Your Honor,

asr-002403
02:28:24.378 --> 02:28:26.480
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: as in prior projects, no?

asr-002404
02:28:26.480 --> 02:28:28.582
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: There have been projects that

asr-002405
02:28:28.582 --> 02:28:30.684
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: there are engagements by the government

asr-002406
02:28:30.684 --> 02:28:32.786
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: entering into

asr-002407
02:28:32.786 --> 02:28:35.939
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: various contractual agreements

asr-002408
02:28:35.939 --> 02:28:38.040
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: with the private sector

asr-002409
02:28:38.040 --> 02:28:40.142
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: and it would be possible, no,

asr-002410
02:28:40.142 --> 02:28:41.193
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: it would be possible

asr-002411
02:28:41.193 --> 02:28:44.346
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: that private funds might be used

asr-002412
02:28:44.346 --> 02:28:46.448
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: to procure portions

asr-002413
02:28:46.448 --> 02:28:48.550
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: of the right-of-way, Your Honor.

asr-002414
02:28:48.560 --> 02:28:53.288
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: So, it's possible that you can use

asr-002415
02:28:53.288 --> 02:28:55.160
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: private funds to pay

asr-002416
02:28:55.160 --> 02:28:57.969
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: just compensation?

asr-002417
02:28:57.969 --> 02:28:59.841
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: It's...

asr-002418
02:28:59.841 --> 02:29:05.702
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I'll be direct with the Secretary.

asr-002419
02:29:05.702 --> 02:29:08.511
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I raised this in the 18th Congress.

asr-002420
02:29:08.511 --> 02:29:09.447
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Kasi sa amin,

asr-002421
02:29:09.447 --> 02:29:12.256
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: NIA exercises expropriation.

asr-002422
02:29:12.256 --> 02:29:14.128
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: They acquired property

asr-002423
02:29:14.128 --> 02:29:16.000
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: of farmers around

asr-002424
02:29:16.000 --> 02:29:17.873
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: the Magat Dam

asr-002425
02:29:17.873 --> 02:29:19.745
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: for public use.

asr-002426
02:29:19.745 --> 02:29:20.681
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: But the one who paid it

asr-002427
02:29:20.681 --> 02:29:22.554
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: is a private corporation.

asr-002428
02:29:22.554 --> 02:29:29.950
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Pwede ba 'yon?

asr-002429
02:29:29.960 --> 02:29:32.118
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: I don't think that's within the realm

asr-002430
02:29:32.118 --> 02:29:35.354
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: of our legal system, Your Honor.

asr-002431
02:29:35.354 --> 02:29:37.512
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Private funds cannot be used

asr-002432
02:29:37.512 --> 02:29:39.670
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: in that manner, Your Honor.

asr-002433
02:29:39.680 --> 02:29:42.085
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: That, in that case,

asr-002434
02:29:42.085 --> 02:29:44.491
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: is the private...

asr-002435
02:29:44.491 --> 02:29:46.896
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: is the public...

asr-002436
02:29:46.896 --> 02:29:48.099
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: public corporation

asr-002437
02:29:48.099 --> 02:29:50.505
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: or the public entity

asr-002438
02:29:50.505 --> 02:29:52.910
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: liable for anything?

asr-002439
02:29:52.920 --> 02:29:59.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes. We have to check the circumstances, Your Honor. Yes, possible po, Your Honor.

asr-002440
02:29:59.439 --> 02:30:09.389
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: What would be the liability, any administrative or criminal liability?

asr-002441
02:30:09.399 --> 02:30:20.790
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Your Honor, if you may, we need additional factual circumstances to make a determination on that matter, Your Honor.

asr-002442
02:30:20.800 --> 02:30:25.016
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Well, I'm laying the facts. The facts are simple.

asr-002443
02:30:27.412 --> 02:30:42.667
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: They raised the level of the dam to the level that it acquired private properties, supposedly for irrigation.

asr-002444
02:30:43.698 --> 02:30:59.773
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: But when they were supposed to pay for the just compensation, it was a private corporation who wanted to pay and paid them, pero hindi patas.

asr-002445
02:30:59.773 --> 02:31:08.795
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Is there anything wrong in that case?

asr-002446
02:31:10.403 --> 02:31:11.070
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Secretary? Ano 'yung right—anong ROW 'yun?

asr-002447
02:31:11.080 --> 02:31:21.705
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Under the existing ROW Act, Your Honor, if I get the briefing right, what will be used for expropriation should be public funds.

asr-002448
02:31:22.586 --> 02:31:32.150
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So any violation of that law would make the person liable if it violates that particular law, Your Honor.

asr-002449
02:31:32.160 --> 02:31:33.844
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: The agency, the agency—

asr-002450
02:31:34.566 --> 02:31:37.903
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: NIA violated the law.

asr-002451
02:31:38.926 --> 02:31:48.037
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: What is the crime? What is the liability of NIA, administratively or criminally?

asr-002452
02:31:48.488 --> 02:31:50.322
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: That's what I'm asking.

asr-002453
02:31:50.924 --> 02:31:53.269
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Kasi hindi inayos 'to, eh. Oo, hindi kasi...

asr-002454
02:31:53.279 --> 02:32:03.070
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Your Honor, we, my apologies, but if you will allow the department, we can give you the proper briefing on that.

asr-002455
02:32:03.080 --> 02:32:06.190
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: We can give you the report on that.

asr-002456
02:32:06.200 --> 02:32:10.030
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: But for any action of an individual, it can arise...

asr-002459
02:32:10.040 --> 02:32:13.401
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: It can arise to criminal or administrative liability.

asr-002460
02:32:13.619 --> 02:32:14.232
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: That's possible.

asr-002461
02:32:14.607 --> 02:32:18.344
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: And also from a criminal act, a civil liability will also ensue.

asr-002462
02:32:18.957 --> 02:32:26.687
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So based on the particular act, Your Honor, we need to see with more particularity the circumstances, Your Honor.

asr-002463
02:32:27.023 --> 02:32:28.190
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: My apologies, Your Honor.

asr-002464
02:32:28.200 --> 02:32:32.510
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Okay, I will just ask perhaps your office for your legal opinion.

asr-002465
02:32:32.520 --> 02:32:35.550
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Because the farmers are complaining.

asr-002466
02:32:35.560 --> 02:32:38.230
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I brought this out in the 18th Congress.

asr-002467
02:32:38.240 --> 02:32:38.790
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I told them.

asr-002468
02:32:38.800 --> 02:32:54.510
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Ayusin ninyo 'yan. Pero hindi inayos hanggang ngayon. So the farmers are coming back. Ang ginagawa nila kasi, binabarat 'yung iba, binabayaran 'yung iba. Hindi naman puwede 'yun, 'di ba?

asr-002469
02:32:54.520 --> 02:32:58.770
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes, Your Honor. The ultimate basis for everything is fairness and justice.

asr-002470
02:32:58.770 --> 02:33:04.481
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So flowing from that, if there's something unfair, probably there's a violation of the law.

asr-002471
02:33:04.481 --> 02:33:11.715
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So if it's an unfair act, then there's a law violated.

asr-002472
02:33:12.381 --> 02:33:15.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So we'll just coordinate with your office, Your Honor.

asr-002473
02:33:15.439 --> 02:33:17.543
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: Okay, I'll just write your office.

asr-002474
02:33:17.709 --> 02:33:23.630
Rep. Solomon R. Chungalao: I will limit myself to allow my other colleagues to be able to ask questions.

asr-002475
02:33:23.640 --> 02:33:25.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Thank you very much.

asr-002476
