03:14:11.190 --> 03:14:13.213
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Solgen. Lastly,

asr-003380
03:14:13.401 --> 03:14:15.362
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Mr. Chair, I would like to make a

asr-003381
03:14:15.362 --> 03:14:17.156
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: manifestation of full support

asr-003382
03:14:17.156 --> 03:14:18.950
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: for the increase of budget

asr-003383
03:14:18.950 --> 03:14:21.098
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: of Department of Justice,

asr-003384
03:14:21.328 --> 03:14:22.913
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: siyempre po kay Sec Vida.

asr-003385
03:14:23.539 --> 03:14:24.936
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: And also, I would like to

asr-003386
03:14:24.936 --> 03:14:27.982
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: advocate for the increase of MOOE

asr-003387
03:14:27.982 --> 03:14:29.358
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: for Solgen.

asr-003388
03:14:29.984 --> 03:14:32.091
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Sana po mangyari na po itong mga wishlist

asr-003389
03:14:32.091 --> 03:14:34.010
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ninyo. Looking forward po

asr-003390
03:14:34.010 --> 03:14:35.262
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: for 2027,

asr-003391
03:14:36.096 --> 03:14:37.848
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: mas ma-improve pa po natin ang services

asr-003392
03:14:37.848 --> 03:14:39.892
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: ng Office of the Solicitor General

asr-003393
03:14:39.892 --> 03:14:42.229
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: and the rest of the Department of Justice.

asr-003394
03:14:42.479 --> 03:14:43.222
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Maraming maraming salamat po.

asr-003395
03:14:43.222 --> 03:14:43.473
Rep. Ma. Cristina Talavera Lopez: Thank you po.

asr-003396
03:14:43.943 --> 03:14:45.645
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Cong. Tina Talavera Lopez.

asr-003397
03:14:46.610 --> 03:14:48.311
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line from the minority

asr-003398
03:14:48.311 --> 03:14:49.627
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: representative.

asr-003399
03:14:49.715 --> 03:14:51.807
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Representative Perci Cendana.

asr-003400
03:14:56.279 --> 03:14:57.477
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-003401
03:14:57.581 --> 03:15:01.072
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Good afternoon, Secretary Vida and to the DOJ family.

asr-003402
03:15:01.558 --> 03:15:04.267
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: I'd just like to follow through, if I may, Mr. Secretary,

asr-003403
03:15:04.840 --> 03:15:10.190
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: on the issues that were raised, particularly on online sexual abuse and exploitation of children,

asr-003404
03:15:10.467 --> 03:15:13.439
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: kasama po iyong CSEAEM at iyong ating massive budget cuts.

asr-003405
03:15:13.439 --> 03:15:16.609
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: May I direct the questions po? Diretso na po ba kay Asec. Lapuz?

asr-003406
03:15:17.600 --> 03:15:18.559
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Yes, of course, Your Honor.

asr-003407
03:15:19.000 --> 03:15:20.284
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-003408
03:15:22.233 --> 03:15:30.603
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Secretary Vida, given the massive cuts in your programs and budget items,

asr-003409
03:15:31.199 --> 03:15:34.716
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: what does this mean in terms of you doing your job?

asr-003410
03:15:35.390 --> 03:15:42.696
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kasi nakita ko po ang range po ng cuts ay from 71%, 58%,

asr-003411
03:15:42.696 --> 03:15:45.521
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: 14%. So ano po ang magiging epekto nito sa ating trabaho?

asr-003412
03:15:46.960 --> 03:15:49.172
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Thank you, Your Honor, for the question.

asr-003413
03:15:50.202 --> 03:15:50.928
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: First of all,

asr-003414
03:15:51.080 --> 03:15:59.019
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: mapapabagal iyong national response po natin against OSAEC and against trafficking.

asr-003415
03:15:59.528 --> 03:16:04.252
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Meron po kaming nakalatag ngayon na National Strategic Action Plan.

asr-003416
03:16:04.350 --> 03:16:05.644
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: It's a four-year plan.

asr-003417
03:16:06.154 --> 03:16:08.780
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: And with the massive budget cuts,

asr-003418
03:16:09.074 --> 03:16:15.523
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: meron pong mga priority programs na maaaring hindi ma-implement.

asr-003419
03:16:15.523 --> 03:16:19.679
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: And alam naman po natin, pag sinasabi nating strategic action plan,

asr-003420
03:16:20.482 --> 03:16:22.423
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: kailangan naka-step by step iyan.

asr-003421
03:16:22.560 --> 03:16:26.284
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Hindi ka maka-proceed to other important programs

asr-003422
03:16:26.284 --> 03:16:28.597
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: unless you build the foundations first.

asr-003423
03:16:28.597 --> 03:16:32.792
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Ang maganda po dito, despite limitations in resources,

asr-003424
03:16:33.439 --> 03:16:38.865
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: nakabuo na po tayo ng magandang mechanism for local task forces

asr-003425
03:16:38.865 --> 03:16:42.282
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: to do responses on the ground.

asr-003426
03:16:42.924 --> 03:16:48.930
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Pero kulang na kulang po iyong capability by these local task forces

asr-003427
03:16:48.930 --> 03:16:50.007
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: because,

asr-003428
03:16:50.815 --> 03:16:55.185
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: una, kulang po iyong budget allocations.

asr-003429
03:16:55.185 --> 03:16:56.324
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: At the same time,

asr-003430
03:16:56.924 --> 03:16:58.353
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: fragmented pa rin po iyong response.

asr-003431
03:17:00.259 --> 03:17:03.199
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Kailangan itawid iyong national program

asr-003432
03:17:03.199 --> 03:17:09.040
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: at i-localize po siya sa mga strategic local governments

asr-003433
03:17:09.040 --> 03:17:12.270
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: and local task forces that are already in place.

asr-003434
03:17:12.395 --> 03:17:15.377
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: However, if we don't have enough resources

asr-003435
03:17:15.377 --> 03:17:18.276
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: to support the operations of these mechanisms,

asr-003436
03:17:18.276 --> 03:17:20.347
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: mapapabagal po iyong rescue operations.

asr-003437
03:17:21.880 --> 03:17:25.681
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Important po iyong rescue operations

asr-003438
03:17:25.681 --> 03:17:29.060
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: because this leads to victim identification.

asr-003439
03:17:29.377 --> 03:17:31.066
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: If we identify victims,

asr-003440
03:17:31.214 --> 03:17:34.360
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: then we know how to get to them,

asr-003441
03:17:34.445 --> 03:17:35.247
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: where they are,

asr-003442
03:17:35.395 --> 03:17:36.092
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: who they are.

asr-003443
03:17:36.177 --> 03:17:37.254
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: We can rescue them.

asr-003444
03:17:37.507 --> 03:17:42.280
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: We can take a child out of an abusive situation

asr-003445
03:17:42.280 --> 03:17:43.399
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: the soonest possible time.

asr-003446
03:17:43.800 --> 03:17:47.459
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: So we are really advocating po to, at the very least,

asr-003447
03:17:47.459 --> 03:17:52.351
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: restore the budget levels of NCC-OSAEC and IACAT to the 2026 levels.

asr-003448
03:17:52.840 --> 03:17:56.529
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair, I am extremely alarmed

asr-003449
03:17:56.529 --> 03:17:58.935
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: at the scenario we're looking at

asr-003450
03:17:58.935 --> 03:18:02.920
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: to the budget levels for the special enforcement

asr-003451
03:18:02.920 --> 03:18:04.971
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: and protection sub-program

asr-003452
03:18:04.971 --> 03:18:07.338
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: remain at the current levels as proposed.

asr-003453
03:18:08.127 --> 03:18:10.672
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ibig sabihin po nito, parang sinasabi natin,

asr-003454
03:18:10.869 --> 03:18:13.848
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: okay lang na hindi ma-rescue ang mga biktima.

asr-003455
03:18:14.479 --> 03:18:17.487
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Okay lang na bumagal ang ating proseso

asr-003456
03:18:17.487 --> 03:18:19.650
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: para tiyakin na maililigtas sila.

asr-003457
03:18:19.650 --> 03:18:21.381
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: We usually say that the budget

asr-003458
03:18:21.381 --> 03:18:22.383
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: is the most concrete,

asr-003459
03:18:22.403 --> 03:18:25.844
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: expression of an administration's priority.

asr-003460
03:18:25.844 --> 03:18:29.521
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So ibig sabihin po ba nito dito sa massive budget cuts na ito,

asr-003461
03:18:29.521 --> 03:18:35.420
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: hindi priority ng gobyerno ang pagliligtas sa mga biktima ng OSAEC.

asr-003462
03:18:35.420 --> 03:18:40.591
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Hindi priority ng gobyerno ang pag-rescue sa lalong madaling panahon

asr-003463
03:18:40.591 --> 03:18:45.015
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: sa pinakamabilis na paraan ito pong mga biktima po.

asr-003464
03:18:45.015 --> 03:18:51.405
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nito pong napakalaking, masasabi nating, sindikato

asr-003465
03:18:51.405 --> 03:18:52.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na nag-ooperate.

asr-003466
03:18:52.880 --> 03:18:55.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Earlier you mentioned that now we're not just talking about individuals

asr-003467
03:18:55.880 --> 03:18:59.380
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: but we're also talking about how AI is being used.

asr-003468
03:18:59.380 --> 03:19:00.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: With this massive budget cuts,

asr-003469
03:19:00.880 --> 03:19:04.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: how will you be able to respond to this much bigger problem?

asr-003470
03:19:05.880 --> 03:19:10.004
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: We need to catch up, sir, on our mechanisms.

asr-003471
03:19:10.004 --> 03:19:12.581
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Dahil nga po, constantly evolving

asr-003472
03:19:12.581 --> 03:19:16.705
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: and nagiging mas complicated yung modus operandi

asr-003473
03:19:16.705 --> 03:19:20.829
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: ng mga gumagawa po ng illegal recruitment, for example,

asr-003474
03:19:20.829 --> 03:19:21.695
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: or grooming,

asr-003475
03:19:21.695 --> 03:19:25.303
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: na-mention po kanina ni Secretary of Justice

asr-003476
03:19:25.303 --> 03:19:32.520
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: iyong groomers behind iyong mga nihilistic violent extremism incidents po.

asr-003477
03:19:32.520 --> 03:19:39.394
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: Now we don't even need an actual person conducting the enticement of our youth.

asr-003478
03:19:39.394 --> 03:19:43.813
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: It could be an AI agent doing that.

asr-003479
03:19:43.813 --> 03:19:50.687
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: And if we don't put in place the foundations of our IT infrastructure

asr-003480
03:19:50.687 --> 03:19:57.561
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: for the proper, timely, and commensurate response to the threat,

asr-003481
03:19:57.561 --> 03:20:01.980
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: the AI po being used to perpetrate these crimes,

asr-003482
03:20:01.980 --> 03:20:03.453
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: that is the threat.

asr-003483
03:20:03.453 --> 03:20:11.800
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: And we need to provide for a corresponding response to the threat.

asr-003484
03:20:11.800 --> 03:20:16.308
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: So we need to consider yung constantly evolving mechanisms po

asr-003485
03:20:16.308 --> 03:20:18.562
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: of how these crimes are being perpetrated.

asr-003486
03:20:18.562 --> 03:20:22.618
DOJ Assistant Secretary Michelle Anne Lapuz: For us to be able to be one, two, three steps ahead of the threats.

asr-003487
03:20:22.618 --> 03:20:23.520
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-003488
03:20:23.520 --> 03:20:24.720
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Thank you, Usec.

asr-003489
03:20:24.720 --> 03:20:26.520
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Asec.

asr-003490
03:20:26.520 --> 03:20:31.315
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So hindi lamang po pala yung mga masasamang elementong ito ang threat

asr-003491
03:20:31.315 --> 03:20:33.712
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: sa kaligtasan ng ating mga kabataan.

asr-003492
03:20:33.712 --> 03:20:36.589
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Yung mismo pong budget na pinutol at tinanggal

asr-003493
03:20:36.589 --> 03:20:38.986
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: is also a threat to the safety of our children.

asr-003494
03:20:38.986 --> 03:20:43.301
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Again, we support you in restoring your budget to the 2026 levels.

asr-003495
03:20:43.301 --> 03:20:47.137
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And kahit po kami ay bahagi ng minority, kasama niyo po kami.

asr-003496
03:20:47.617 --> 03:20:51.932
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: We support your advocacy para po sa lalong madaling panahon ma-restore to 2026 levels.

asr-003497
03:20:51.932 --> 03:20:55.288
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Deserve po ng ating mga bata na maprotektahan.

asr-003498
03:20:55.288 --> 03:20:57.685
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: At yung mga nasa peligro na po,

asr-003499
03:20:57.685 --> 03:21:03.439
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: deserve na deserve nila ang immediate rescue at assistance.

asr-003500
03:21:03.439 --> 03:21:12.000
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair, let me direct my next set of questions to the Bureau of Immigration.

asr-003501
03:21:12.000 --> 03:21:13.600
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Magandang hapon po, Commissioner Viado.

asr-003502
03:21:13.600 --> 03:21:16.720
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Magandang hapon po, Congressman Cendana.

asr-003503
03:21:16.720 --> 03:21:17.678
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Magandang hapon po.

asr-003504
03:21:17.678 --> 03:21:19.595
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ito po ay tungkol po sa usapin ng

asr-003505
03:21:19.595 --> 03:21:25.346
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nung mga paggamit ng blacklist at entry restrictions as a political tool.

asr-003506
03:21:25.346 --> 03:21:28.221
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nakita po natin yan noong nakaraang administrasyon.

asr-003507
03:21:28.221 --> 03:21:33.971
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ginamit itong mga blacklist at entry restrictions laban sa mga advocates,

asr-003508
03:21:33.971 --> 03:21:38.763
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: laban sa mga aktibista, at laban sa mismong kinatawan ng United Nations

asr-003509
03:21:38.763 --> 03:21:40.680
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: na human rights advocate.

asr-003510
03:21:40.680 --> 03:21:44.737
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Ginamit ito in aid of violence and impunity.

asr-003511
03:21:44.737 --> 03:21:48.794
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Noong 2026 po, sinabi ng Amnesty International Philippines,

asr-003512
03:21:48.794 --> 03:21:54.880
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: nananatiling mayroong entry ban si Amnesty International Secretary General Agnès Callamard

asr-003513
03:21:54.880 --> 03:22:00.965
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: as a result of her previous work as, again, UN Special Rapporteur on Extrajudicial Killings.

asr-003514
03:22:00.965 --> 03:22:07.051
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nagsimula po ang ban na ito noong 2018, bunga ng public attack ni former President Rodrigo Duterte.

asr-003515
03:22:07.051 --> 03:22:12.122
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Kaya mahalaga pong malaman natin meron po bang sapat na safeguards ang BI

asr-003516
03:22:12.122 --> 03:22:17.193
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: upang matiyak na hindi ito nagagamit arbitrarily, hindi ito naweweaponize,

asr-003517
03:22:17.193 --> 03:22:23.279
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: at para po tiyakin na hindi ito ginagamit laban sa human rights work and peaceful advocacy.

asr-003518
03:22:23.279 --> 03:22:32.960
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: The first question, Mr. Chair: maaari po bang kumpirmahin ng BI ang kasalukuyang status ng entry restriction kay Ms. Agnès Callamard?

asr-003519
03:22:32.960 --> 03:22:50.000
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: If I may confirm with my colleague, Your Honor.

asr-003520
03:22:50.000 --> 03:22:57.667
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honors, ang lahat po ng desisyon ng Bureau of Immigration ay dumaan po sa proseso, unang-una.

asr-003521
03:22:57.667 --> 03:22:58.482
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang information po na nakalap namin ay hindi lang po galing sa vetting na ginawa ng Bureau of Immigration,

asr-003524
03:22:59.297 --> 03:23:00.926
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: but galing po sa ibang mga ahensya,

asr-003525
03:23:00.926 --> 03:23:01.741
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: dito po and internationally.

asr-003526
03:23:01.741 --> 03:23:05.000
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We refer to Interpol lists, we refer to fugitive status of individuals bago po kami umaksyon.

asr-003527
03:23:05.000 --> 03:23:11.165
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And internally, Your Honor, bago po kami mag-issue ng any blacklist, dumadaan po iyan sa proseso

asr-003528
03:23:11.165 --> 03:23:17.331
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: kung saan ang legal division, ang amin hong mga abogado sa legal division,

asr-003529
03:23:17.331 --> 03:23:20.414
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and eventually iyong mga Board of Special Inquiry at Board of Commissioners.

asr-003530
03:23:20.845 --> 03:23:26.887
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Dinadaanan po iyan ng hindi lang maikling proseso pero mahaba-haba po, Your Honor.

asr-003531
03:23:27.319 --> 03:23:33.399
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So we can assure po, Your Honors, na any decision, any order concerning any blacklist

asr-003532
03:23:33.399 --> 03:23:37.204
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: ay dumaan po sa tamang proseso at legal na pamamaraan po, Your Honor.

asr-003533
03:23:37.204 --> 03:23:45.519
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi po arbitrary, hindi po

asr-003534
03:23:45.720 --> 03:23:49.198
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: at the behest of any individual. Ito po ay ginagawa po sa level po ng aming bureau.

asr-003535
03:23:49.198 --> 03:23:56.453
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: So the question again, Mr. Chair, ano po ang status ng entry restriction kay Ms. Agnès Callamard?

asr-003536
03:23:56.560 --> 03:24:05.937
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Again po, si Ms. Agnès Callamard po, sigurado ako wala po iyan sa blacklist ng Interpol.

asr-003537
03:24:05.937 --> 03:24:15.421
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: She is former United Nations Special Rapporteur on Extrajudicial Killings.

asr-003538
03:24:16.960 --> 03:24:20.515
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We are confirming po iyong status ni Special Rapporteur Callamard.

asr-003539
03:24:20.885 --> 03:24:25.610
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But kung base po dito sa information po na nakalap namin ngayon, galing po dito sa honorable body na ito,

asr-003540
03:24:25.625 --> 03:24:28.868
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: we are willing to also review the status of the Special Rapporteur.

asr-003541
03:24:29.120 --> 03:24:37.994
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Because we are in favor of human rights, we are in favor of other persons from other countries coming into our country

asr-003542
03:24:37.994 --> 03:24:42.485
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and to see how we have gone forward as far as human rights are concerned, Your Honor.

asr-003543
03:24:43.319 --> 03:24:46.757
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Mr. Chair, thank you very much, Commissioner Viado, for that response.

asr-003544
03:24:47.164 --> 03:24:50.195
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: And we welcome your willingness to review your guidelines, no?

asr-003545
03:24:50.195 --> 03:24:55.321
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Lalo na po pagdating sa mga human rights defenders, international advocates, journalists,

asr-003546
03:24:55.525 --> 03:24:58.027
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: academics, and especially UN officials.

asr-003547
03:24:58.800 --> 03:25:05.146
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Sa proseso po noong pag-review, inaasahan po natin na hindi na ito magagamit as a political weapon

asr-003548
03:25:05.146 --> 03:25:08.728
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: against voices of dissent, against voices of human rights.

asr-003549
03:25:08.960 --> 03:25:14.330
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: Nagawa na po ito noong madilim na panahon ng Rehimen Duterte, huwag na po nating hayaang maulit.

asr-003550
03:25:14.527 --> 03:25:18.165
Rep. Percival "Perci" Cendaña: That will be all, Mr. Chair. Marami pong salamat sa DOJ family.

asr-003551
03:25:18.560 --> 03:25:19.441
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thank you rin po, Your Honor.

asr-003552
03:25:19.840 --> 03:25:21.031
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Congressman Cendana.

asr-003553
03:25:21.618 --> 03:25:22.952
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line from the majority.

asr-003554
03:25:26.000 --> 03:25:30.790
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Rep. Ann Matibag.

asr-003555
03:25:34.593 --> 03:25:39.870
Rep. Ann Matibag: Ann Matibag. Thank you. Um, I just want to interject also,

asr-003556
03:25:39.880 --> 03:25:45.070
Rep. Ann Matibag: no, after what my good friend Cong. Perci

asr-003557
03:25:45.080 --> 03:25:50.030
Rep. Ann Matibag: has conveyed, especially to the OSAEC cases. We are really disheartened on

asr-003558
03:25:50.040 --> 03:25:55.429
Rep. Ann Matibag: what happened with the deduction of your budget, and

asr-003559
03:25:55.439 --> 03:26:00.389
Rep. Ann Matibag: with the OSAEC cases, we were more surprised

asr-003560
03:26:00.399 --> 03:26:05.309
Rep. Ann Matibag: that much in the Department, 'yung mga law enforcement pa,

asr-003561
03:26:05.319 --> 03:26:10.710
Rep. Ann Matibag: 'yung mas nabawasan din, no, like the Bureau of Immigration and the National

asr-003562
03:26:10.720 --> 03:26:14.910
Rep. Ann Matibag: Bureau of Investigation. So I just want to commend Mr.

asr-003563
03:26:14.920 --> 03:26:20.030
Rep. Ann Matibag: Chair, Secretary Vida, and your whole team.

asr-003564
03:26:20.040 --> 03:26:25.790
Rep. Ann Matibag: We were in New York, in the United Nations, last March. I am with Usec. Majken Anika, and

asr-003565
03:26:25.800 --> 03:26:30.590
Rep. Ann Matibag: I want to commend their program, which is the Revised CANE+D

asr-003566
03:26:30.600 --> 03:26:36.030
Rep. Ann Matibag: Protocol, which is intended to provide a more standardized and coordinated

asr-003567
03:26:36.040 --> 03:26:41.269
Rep. Ann Matibag: way of handling cases such as this of violence against women and children.

asr-003568
03:26:41.279 --> 03:26:45.990
Rep. Ann Matibag: So this emphasizes the clarity on the responsibilities of the agencies involved,

asr-003569
03:26:46.000 --> 03:26:51.150
Rep. Ann Matibag: coordinating among them, and a more child-sensitive approach to investigation

asr-003570
03:26:51.160 --> 03:26:56.750
Rep. Ann Matibag: and prosecution. So this is not just a policy in paper. I just want to

asr-003571
03:26:56.760 --> 03:27:01.670
Rep. Ann Matibag: tell—and I'm just so proud of this program of the Department

asr-003572
03:27:01.680 --> 03:27:06.710
Rep. Ann Matibag: of Justice—and this has already begun

asr-003573
03:27:06.720 --> 03:27:12.269
Rep. Ann Matibag: bringing the Revised Protocol to the local level. I remember when

asr-003574
03:27:12.279 --> 03:27:16.910
Rep. Ann Matibag: my group, my social organization, Zonta Club of Laguna,

asr-003575
03:27:16.920 --> 03:27:22.229
Rep. Ann Matibag: went to the office of Secretary Vida, and he was very happy to tell us that

asr-003576
03:27:22.239 --> 03:27:27.389
Rep. Ann Matibag: this is not just laws. This is not just a memorandum or any piece of paper or

asr-003577
03:27:27.399 --> 03:27:32.429
Rep. Ann Matibag: a policy, but they already launched nationally in August

asr-003578
03:27:32.439 --> 03:27:37.469
Rep. Ann Matibag: 2025, followed by the provincial implementation in Cavite in

asr-003579
03:27:37.479 --> 03:27:41.670
Rep. Ann Matibag: March 2026 and in Cebu in July 2026.

asr-003580
03:27:41.680 --> 03:27:47.309
Rep. Ann Matibag: So for me, this is exactly the kind of program that deserves support in the

asr-003581
03:27:47.319 --> 03:27:53.070
Rep. Ann Matibag: 2027 budget, especially I'm the chairperson of the Committee on Women and Gender

asr-003582
03:27:53.080 --> 03:27:58.150
Rep. Ann Matibag: Equality, and I'm with Cong. Sarah Elago and Cong. Perci,

asr-003583
03:27:58.160 --> 03:28:02.950
Rep. Ann Matibag: who are members of my committee. Rest assured that I just want to manifest my

asr-003584
03:28:02.960 --> 03:28:08.630
Rep. Ann Matibag: support, that we will make sure that your budget will not only be increased,

asr-003585
03:28:08.640 --> 03:28:13.790
Rep. Ann Matibag: but with what you wish and hope for to have, especially to the department

asr-003586
03:28:13.800 --> 03:28:18.710
Rep. Ann Matibag: of the wife of Cong. Keith—she's the director—so we

asr-003587
03:28:18.720 --> 03:28:23.590
Rep. Ann Matibag: are in support of that. And maybe before the plenary session, we can

asr-003588
03:28:23.600 --> 03:28:29.030
Rep. Ann Matibag: huddle and think things together, and maybe discuss on

asr-003589
03:28:29.040 --> 03:28:33.910
Rep. Ann Matibag: how we can really explain

asr-003590
03:28:33.920 --> 03:28:39.349
Rep. Ann Matibag: and discuss this budget that we need to really

asr-003591
03:28:39.359 --> 03:28:44.309
Rep. Ann Matibag: bring it back to the DOJ's wish. And I am very happy to

asr-003592
03:28:44.319 --> 03:28:49.030
Rep. Ann Matibag: see everyone here. DOJ, special po kayo dahil

asr-003593
03:28:49.040 --> 03:28:54.389
Rep. Ann Matibag: ako'y pinalaki ng isang fiscal—ang tatay ko.

asr-003594
03:28:54.399 --> 03:28:59.550
Rep. Ann Matibag: Especially now that NBI here is very,

asr-003595
03:28:59.560 --> 03:29:04.710
Rep. Ann Matibag: very responsive to the needs of being a law enforcement for women and children.

asr-003596
03:29:04.720 --> 03:29:09.968
Rep. Ann Matibag: So, maraming-maraming salamat po. You have my support and respect. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-003597
03:29:11.099 --> 03:29:15.750
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Cong. Ann Matibag, sa suporta po sa ating pong ahensya.

asr-003598
03:29:15.760 --> 03:29:20.853
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line from the minority, Representative Leila de Lima.

asr-003599
03:29:24.720 --> 03:29:26.359
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-003600
03:29:26.359 --> 03:29:27.371
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Good afternoon to my colleagues.

asr-003601
03:29:27.493 --> 03:29:31.986
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And good afternoon to Secretary Vida and the DOJ family.

asr-003602
03:29:31.986 --> 03:29:34.010
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kumusta po kayo?

asr-003603
03:29:34.010 --> 03:29:35.021
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Okay.

asr-003604
03:29:35.021 --> 03:29:44.048
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Let me start by manifesting not only my support for the budget, the department-wide budget

asr-003605
03:29:44.048 --> 03:29:49.512
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: of the DOJ, but also support for the push for the restoration of some of the areas of

asr-003606
03:29:49.512 --> 03:29:50.160
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: the DOJ.

asr-003613
03:29:50.160 --> 03:29:55.819
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: some of the budget that was cut, including the ones for OSAEC and also

asr-003614
03:29:55.819 --> 03:30:04.095
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: for IACAT. And we do note very much the significant cuts, of course, in the

asr-003615
03:30:04.095 --> 03:30:12.553
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: DOJ-wide budget, a 61.82% cut, and then the biggest among the agencies is the

asr-003616
03:30:12.553 --> 03:30:22.168
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Bucor by 84.18% cut. I'm talking about the NEP as against the proposed budget

asr-003617
03:30:22.168 --> 03:30:35.596
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: and then also NBI as 65.84%. So ang gusto ko pong i-ano ngayon, lalo na dyan sa Bucor and sa NBI, if you wish to

asr-003618
03:30:35.596 --> 03:30:42.127
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: insist about or for more in your wish list for increase in the budget, please

asr-003619
03:30:42.127 --> 03:30:42.573
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: tell us.

asr-003621
03:30:43.486 --> 03:30:50.058
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: But specific items in the budget for Bucor, for DOJ, for NBI, and even the

asr-003622
03:30:50.058 --> 03:30:58.172
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: others, OSG and even PAO, so that we can help you out, at least put back the

asr-003623
03:30:58.172 --> 03:31:05.656
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: priority, your priority programs that were actually cut in the NEP.

asr-003625
03:31:06.265 --> 03:31:15.372
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Now, I wish to direct my questions first to BI.

asr-003627
03:31:16.224 --> 03:31:22.898
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: then to Bucor and the DOJ proper.

asr-003628
03:31:25.920 --> 03:31:29.619
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: I would wish also to pursue further the case of Dr. Calamard.

asr-003629
03:31:29.912 --> 03:31:30.351
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, ma'am.

asr-003630
03:31:30.937 --> 03:31:36.046
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: It struck me what you said, that it was not at any behest when you make any blacklisting.

asr-003631
03:31:36.138 --> 03:31:36.797
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, ma'am.

asr-003632
03:31:36.797 --> 03:31:40.862
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Sa case ho ba ni Dr. Callamard, ganoon? It was at no one’s behest.

asr-003633
03:31:41.833 --> 03:31:43.280
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As far as I know, Your Honor.

asr-003634
03:31:43.444 --> 03:31:45.166
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: We want to understand further.

asr-003635
03:31:46.576 --> 03:31:49.359
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: What was the legal basis for the blacklisting of Dr. Calamard?

asr-003636
03:31:49.359 --> 03:31:55.119
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Your Honor, based on the record, it was a national security concern, Your Honor.

asr-003637
03:31:55.119 --> 03:31:56.708
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: A national security concern?

asr-003638
03:31:56.708 --> 03:31:57.701
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes.

asr-003639
03:31:57.701 --> 03:32:01.673
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Do you have any specific explanation for that?

asr-003640
03:32:01.673 --> 03:32:03.659
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: National security concern?

asr-003641
03:32:03.659 --> 03:32:05.645
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Meron ho bang security threat?

asr-003642
03:32:05.645 --> 03:32:07.631
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: There was no crime committed, correct?

asr-003643
03:32:07.631 --> 03:32:09.617
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: There was no crime committed?

asr-003644
03:32:09.617 --> 03:32:11.604
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As far as I know, Your Honor, no.

asr-003645
03:32:11.604 --> 03:32:13.590
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And there was no immigration violation?

asr-003646
03:32:13.590 --> 03:32:14.583
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003647
03:32:14.583 --> 03:32:15.615
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Immigration laws violation?

asr-003648
03:32:15.615 --> 03:32:16.609
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003649
03:32:16.609 --> 03:32:17.602
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Immigration laws violation committed.

asr-003650
03:32:17.602 --> 03:32:20.581
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: But what you are saying now is a national security threat.

asr-003651
03:32:20.581 --> 03:32:21.574
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003652
03:32:21.574 --> 03:32:32.497
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: But isn’t she the one who investigated the drug-war killings as the former UN Special Rapporteur on extrajudicial killings?

asr-003653
03:32:32.497 --> 03:32:33.491
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, yes.

asr-003654
03:32:33.491 --> 03:32:39.449
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That is based on the records available, Your Honor, to us at the moment, Your Honor.

asr-003655
03:32:39.449 --> 03:32:44.414
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: I can dig deeper into this matter, Your Honor, because this matter, I think, was...

asr-003656
03:32:45.407 --> 03:32:52.359
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: occurred even before we came into, you know, we were appointed to the Bureau of Immigration.

asr-003657
03:32:52.359 --> 03:32:55.338
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But if...

asr-003658
03:32:55.338 --> 03:33:01.296
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So hanggang ngayon po, hindi ninyo talaga alam exactly kung anong naging basehan?

asr-003659
03:33:01.296 --> 03:33:07.255
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang basehan po is based on reports from a national security agency, Your Honor.

asr-003660
03:33:07.255 --> 03:33:14.206
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But I can give you the details and the other facts and issues concerning this matter.

asr-003661
03:33:15.199 --> 03:33:19.122
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: If you can give us a chance, Your Honor, we can give you a full detailed report on that matter.

asr-003662
03:33:19.122 --> 03:33:23.044
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Hindi ho ba merong motion for reconsideration with respect to that?

asr-003663
03:33:23.044 --> 03:33:29.909
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: As far back as August 2026, there is this motion for reconsideration on the blacklisting of Dr. Calamard.

asr-003664
03:33:29.909 --> 03:33:30.890
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: For the lifting, Your Honor?

asr-003665
03:33:30.890 --> 03:33:34.813
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: For the lifting, for the lifting of the blacklist.

asr-003666
03:33:34.813 --> 03:33:43.639
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And isn’t it that under the BI Omnibus Rules, the commissioner is supposed to resolve a lifting petition within 15 working days?

asr-003667
03:33:44.620 --> 03:33:45.600
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor...

asr-003668
03:33:45.600 --> 03:33:49.523
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Bakit napakatagal na iyong ginagawa ninyong review about the case of Dr. Callamard?

asr-003669
03:33:49.523 --> 03:33:53.446
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, as far as I know, there is no pending matter involving this.

asr-003670
03:33:53.446 --> 03:33:57.368
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But once we get back to the office, Your Honor, we will act on it right away.

asr-003671
03:33:57.368 --> 03:33:59.330
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: How soon can we expect that?

asr-003672
03:33:59.330 --> 03:34:07.175
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Because this is, you know, this matter is being monitored, actually, by certain UN officials.

asr-003673
03:34:07.175 --> 03:34:09.137
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor. We understand, Your Honor.

asr-003674
03:34:09.137 --> 03:34:12.079
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We will act on it right away by tomorrow, Your Honor.

asr-003675
03:34:12.079 --> 03:34:13.059
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Okay.

asr-003676
03:34:14.040 --> 03:34:18.189
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Okay. Doon naman po sa CAIS.

asr-003677
03:34:18.189 --> 03:34:19.227
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That’s the CAIS, Your Honor.

asr-003678
03:34:19.227 --> 03:34:20.264
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: The CAIS.

asr-003679
03:34:20.264 --> 03:34:21.301
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-003680
03:34:21.301 --> 03:34:24.413
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: May pino-propose kayong additional P480 fee.

asr-003681
03:34:24.413 --> 03:34:25.451
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-003682
03:34:25.451 --> 03:34:27.525
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: For the CAISS.

asr-003683
03:34:27.525 --> 03:34:34.787
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Bago ho ninyo na-propose itong fee na ito, was there any alternative funding source being considered?

asr-003684
03:34:34.787 --> 03:34:44.123
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Considering, Your Honor, that this is a public-private partnership program, Your Honor, there was no alternative discussed.

asr-003685
03:34:44.123 --> 03:34:49.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: This is an unsolicited proposal which came from a private proponent.

asr-003686
03:34:49.309 --> 03:35:00.720
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes. So why should—I mean, I’m just wondering—why should the cost of modernizing immigration infrastructure be passed on to the traveling public, even if it’s covered by a PPP?

asr-003687
03:35:00.720 --> 03:35:12.482
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, first and foremost, we need a more integrative program which covers

asr-003688
03:35:12.482 --> 03:35:19.343
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: a border security platform with biometrics, advanced analytics, and passenger information system, actually, to enhance national security and immigration control, Your Honor.

asr-003689
03:35:19.343 --> 03:35:29.145
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: At the moment, there is no particular program which can be funded by the national government at this level.

asr-003690
03:35:29.145 --> 03:35:38.947
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The private proponent proposes to put the capitalization in the amount of 10.7 billion for the next five years.

asr-003691
03:35:38.947 --> 03:35:41.888
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And with the constant upgrade of the system every four years

asr-003692
03:35:41.888 --> 03:35:46.788
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: for the next 20-year period, Your Honor, at no cost to the government.

asr-003693
03:35:46.788 --> 03:35:47.769
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: At no cost to the government.

asr-003694
03:35:47.769 --> 03:35:49.729
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: At no cost to the government, Your Honor.

asr-003695
03:35:49.729 --> 03:35:56.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But you’re still insisting on the P480 fee, because that is what is being demanded.

asr-003696
03:35:56.590 --> 03:36:02.471
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Actually, Your Honor, it is P240 per ticket.

asr-003697
03:36:02.471 --> 03:36:07.372
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So if it’s a round-trip ticket, Your Honor, it’s P480.

asr-003698
03:36:07.372 --> 03:36:09.333
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Compared to other countries, this is way below.

asr-003699
03:36:09.333 --> 03:36:11.293
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: This is actually the practice in other countries.

asr-003700
03:36:11.293 --> 03:36:22.075
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The US, Australia, Singapore, Hong Kong, Japan have been doing this at costs which is much higher than what we are proposing.

asr-003701
03:36:22.075 --> 03:36:31.877
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As a matter of fact, Your Honor, if you can compare, Australia charges about 2,600 pesos per passenger.

asr-003702
03:36:31.877 --> 03:36:34.817
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Singapore charges 2,400.

asr-003703
03:36:34.817 --> 03:36:38.738
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Japan charges about 1,200.

asr-003704
03:36:38.738 --> 03:36:40.698
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hong Kong charges about 1,500.

asr-003705
03:36:40.698 --> 03:36:42.659
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thailand charges about 1,500.

asr-003706
03:36:42.659 --> 03:36:47.560
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And Thailand charges about 1,800, Your Honor.

asr-003707
03:36:47.560 --> 03:36:49.520
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So it stays?

asr-003708
03:36:49.520 --> 03:36:50.565
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: I'm sorry, Your Honor.

asr-003709
03:36:50.565 --> 03:36:52.654
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: The imposition of that fee would stay?

asr-003710
03:36:52.654 --> 03:36:53.698
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: I'm sorry, Your Honor?

asr-003711
03:36:53.698 --> 03:36:55.788
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: It would stay?

asr-003712
03:36:55.788 --> 03:36:57.877
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It is still under review, Your Honor.

asr-003713
03:36:57.877 --> 03:36:59.966
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The contract is still under review, yes.

asr-003714
03:36:59.966 --> 03:37:03.100
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We have not signed any contract.

asr-003715
03:37:03.100 --> 03:37:07.278
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It is still under review by the DOF.

asr-003716
03:37:07.278 --> 03:37:09.368
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The DOJ finished the review already.

asr-003717
03:37:09.368 --> 03:37:16.680
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It is still under review by the Department of Finance and other concerned government agencies, Your Honor.

asr-003718
03:37:16.680 --> 03:37:23.801
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Sa BuCor naman po, nasaan na po ngayon si retired Major General Jovito Palparan?

asr-003719
03:37:23.801 --> 03:37:29.904
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Is he still physically present and confined at the moment at the maximum security compound?

asr-003720
03:37:29.904 --> 03:37:32.956
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: With the permission of our Secretary, yes.

asr-003721
03:37:32.956 --> 03:37:38.042
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ma'am, General Palparan is still with us.

asr-003722
03:37:38.042 --> 03:37:41.094
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: He is confined in New Bilibid Prison.

asr-003723
03:37:41.094 --> 03:37:50.249
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Why were there reports that there were notices addressed to Palparan from the Supreme Court

asr-003724
03:37:50.249 --> 03:37:59.404
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: and then was returned or they were returned unserved because prison authorities refused to receive them,

asr-003725
03:37:59.404 --> 03:38:02.455
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: stating that Palparan was no longer detained there?

asr-003726
03:38:02.455 --> 03:38:07.542
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: In fact, the envelopes of these notices bear a specific annotation.

asr-003727
03:38:07.542 --> 03:38:08.559
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: It says,

asr-003728
03:38:08.559 --> 03:38:11.610
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Moved out, transferred to BuCor, Baguio.

asr-003729
03:38:11.610 --> 03:38:15.679
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: In a separate envelope, moved out to PMA, Baguio.

asr-003730
03:38:15.679 --> 03:38:17.714
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So which is which?

asr-003731
03:38:17.714 --> 03:38:18.731
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: I think...

asr-003732
03:38:18.731 --> 03:38:20.766
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Ang bilis naman po ng five minutes.

asr-003733
03:38:22.800 --> 03:38:26.440
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Hinold ninyo ho ba iyong sasagot?

asr-003734
03:38:26.440 --> 03:38:28.260
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: But anyway, please answer that.

asr-003735
03:38:28.260 --> 03:38:30.079
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Mr. Chair,

asr-003736
03:38:30.079 --> 03:38:33.719
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: General Palparan has never been moved out from New Bilibid Prison.

asr-003737
03:38:33.719 --> 03:38:35.539
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: from New Bilibid Prison.

asr-003738
03:38:35.539 --> 03:38:37.359
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: The one who...

asr-003739
03:38:37.359 --> 03:38:41.310
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: The post-office officials are now being investigated

asr-003740
03:38:41.310 --> 03:38:45.260
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: because they are the ones who are at fault.

asr-003741
03:38:45.260 --> 03:38:50.199
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Sila po ang may kasalanan niyan na nag-report sila na hindi kami in-inform.

asr-003742
03:38:50.199 --> 03:38:52.174
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Kaya po inimbestigahan?

asr-003743
03:38:52.174 --> 03:38:57.112
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Actually, tinanggal na sila at iniimbestigahan po ngayon.

asr-003744
03:38:57.112 --> 03:38:58.100
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So under investigation?

asr-003745
03:38:58.100 --> 03:38:59.087
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Under investigation.

asr-003746
03:38:59.087 --> 03:39:02.050
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kasi bakit sila maglalagay ng ganoong annotation kung hindi totoo?

asr-003747
03:39:02.050 --> 03:39:03.038
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Iyon nga po.

asr-003748
03:39:03.038 --> 03:39:04.026
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Obviously,

asr-003749
03:39:04.026 --> 03:39:06.001
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: oversight po ng mga tauhan iyan.

asr-003750
03:39:06.001 --> 03:39:08.964
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Iyan po iyong problema sa BuCor.

asr-003751
03:39:08.964 --> 03:39:11.927
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: May mga tao diyan talaga na

asr-003752
03:39:11.927 --> 03:39:13.902
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: incorrigible,

asr-003753
03:39:13.902 --> 03:39:14.890
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: recidivist,

asr-003754
03:39:14.890 --> 03:39:17.853
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: iyong mga hindi talaga seryoso sa trabaho.

asr-003755
03:39:17.853 --> 03:39:18.840
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: That is...

asr-003756
03:39:18.840 --> 03:39:20.816
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: You’re talking about the BuCor employees themselves?

asr-003757
03:39:20.816 --> 03:39:21.803
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes. Opo.

asr-003758
03:39:21.803 --> 03:39:22.791
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: That's why I...

asr-003759
03:39:22.791 --> 03:39:27.729
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Kung binabago natin iyong pamamalakad sa mga PDL,

asr-003760
03:39:27.729 --> 03:39:31.680
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: binabago din natin iyong pamamalakad natin sa mga tauhan.

asr-003761
03:39:31.680 --> 03:39:32.829
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: So on your word, Director General,

asr-003762
03:39:32.829 --> 03:39:40.871
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Major General Palparan was never actually transferred to any facility?

asr-003763
03:39:40.871 --> 03:39:42.020
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Never.

asr-003764
03:39:42.020 --> 03:39:43.168
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Never.

asr-003765
03:39:43.168 --> 03:39:46.615
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: May I ask one more question on Bucor?

asr-003766
03:39:46.615 --> 03:39:47.764
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Ask a question.

asr-003767
03:39:47.764 --> 03:39:48.913
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Okay.

asr-003768
03:39:48.913 --> 03:39:52.359
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Although I have several more, but this one.

asr-003769
03:39:52.359 --> 03:39:58.344
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: There’s still illegal drug trade going on within your facilities,

asr-003770
03:39:58.344 --> 03:40:02.334
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: including the New Bilibid Prison, NBP.

asr-003771
03:40:02.334 --> 03:40:03.332
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes.

asr-003772
03:40:03.332 --> 03:40:06.324
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: I must admit, Your Honor.

asr-003773
03:40:06.324 --> 03:40:08.319
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Ano ho ba ang nagiging problema?

asr-003774
03:40:08.319 --> 03:40:11.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ang problema po, iyong mga PDL.

asr-003775
03:40:11.319 --> 03:40:15.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Unang-una, hindi sila na-rehab; dinala sa amin.

asr-003776
03:40:15.319 --> 03:40:18.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So may withdrawal symptoms sila.

asr-003777
03:40:18.319 --> 03:40:20.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Pag tinanong sila ng bibisitahin,

asr-003778
03:40:20.319 --> 03:40:23.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: “Ano bang gusto ninyong ibigay,

asr-003779
03:40:23.319 --> 03:40:24.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: dalhin, pasalubong o pagkain?”

asr-003780
03:40:24.319 --> 03:40:26.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: What do you want to eat?

asr-003781
03:40:26.319 --> 03:40:27.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ang hinihingi po, drugs.

asr-003782
03:40:27.319 --> 03:40:28.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So...

asr-003783
03:40:28.319 --> 03:40:30.319
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: At bakit ho nakakalusot ang drugs?

asr-003784
03:40:30.319 --> 03:40:32.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Kasi po nilalagay sa private parts, eh.

asr-003785
03:40:32.319 --> 03:40:36.319
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: But you have inspection procedures, correct?

asr-003786
03:40:36.319 --> 03:40:37.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes, ma'am.

asr-003787
03:40:37.319 --> 03:40:38.319
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: And based on reports,

asr-003788
03:40:38.319 --> 03:40:42.319
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: you have actually tightened those inspection procedures.

asr-003789
03:40:42.319 --> 03:40:43.319
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes, ma'am.

asr-003790
03:40:43.319 --> 03:40:45.235
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: May nakakalusot pong pailan-ilan

asr-003791
03:40:45.235 --> 03:40:49.068
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: kasi talaga pong nasa private parts.

asr-003792
03:40:49.068 --> 03:40:50.026
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: And then, of course,

asr-003793
03:40:50.026 --> 03:40:54.817
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: may mga tao tayong in connivance with PDLs.

asr-003794
03:40:54.817 --> 03:40:55.775
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So I must admit.

asr-003795
03:40:55.775 --> 03:40:58.649
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Kaya iyan po iyong nire-report ko sa inyo,

asr-003796
03:40:58.649 --> 03:41:00.566
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: na isipin ninyo.

asr-003797
03:41:00.566 --> 03:41:01.524
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Think about it.

asr-003798
03:41:01.524 --> 03:41:02.482
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Isang nurse

asr-003799
03:41:02.482 --> 03:41:05.356
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: nagpasok ng pandesal

asr-003800
03:41:05.356 --> 03:41:07.273
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: na may shabu—

asr-003801
03:41:07.273 --> 03:41:08.231
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: pandesal, pandeshal.

asr-003802
03:41:08.231 --> 03:41:09.189
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Shabu.

asr-003803
03:41:09.189 --> 03:41:10.147
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Pandeshal.

asr-003804
03:41:10.147 --> 03:41:11.105
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So...

asr-003805
03:41:11.105 --> 03:41:12.063
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So nakasuhan po iyon.

asr-003806
03:41:12.063 --> 03:41:13.979
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Tanggal na sa serbisyo iyon.

asr-003807
03:41:13.979 --> 03:41:14.938
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So...

asr-003808
03:41:14.938 --> 03:41:15.896
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ang mga na-dismiss po diyan

asr-003809
03:41:15.896 --> 03:41:17.812
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: ay 43.

asr-003810
03:41:17.812 --> 03:41:20.686
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Suspended, 137.

asr-003811
03:41:20.686 --> 03:41:21.645
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: And of course,

asr-003812
03:41:21.645 --> 03:41:23.561
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: reprimanded, 41.

asr-003813
03:41:23.561 --> 03:41:24.519
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So, ma'am,

asr-003814
03:41:24.519 --> 03:41:26.435
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: hindi po katulad dito ng military.

asr-003815
03:41:26.435 --> 03:41:27.393
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Outright,

asr-003816
03:41:27.393 --> 03:41:28.352
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: puwede ko,

asr-003817
03:41:28.352 --> 03:41:30.268
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: using the Articles of War,

asr-003818
03:41:30.268 --> 03:41:32.184
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: tanggal ka na sa serbisyo.

asr-003819
03:41:32.184 --> 03:41:34.100
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Pero dito po,

asr-003820
03:41:34.100 --> 03:41:35.059
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: But here,

asr-003821
03:41:35.059 --> 03:41:36.017
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: hindi puwede.

asr-003822
03:41:36.017 --> 03:41:36.975
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Dadaan sa Civil Service;

asr-003823
03:41:36.975 --> 03:41:38.891
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: ang daming proseso.

asr-003824
03:41:38.891 --> 03:41:39.849
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Hindi po tayo makakapag-weed out

asr-003825
03:41:39.849 --> 03:41:40.807
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: ng mga bulok na tauhan

asr-003826
03:41:40.807 --> 03:41:41.766
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: that are coming from

asr-003827
03:41:41.766 --> 03:41:44.640
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: ng BuCor kaagad-agad.

asr-003828
03:41:44.640 --> 03:41:46.854
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Follow-up lang po ito.

asr-003829
03:41:46.854 --> 03:41:47.961
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Iyong mga tina-transfer ninyo,

asr-003830
03:41:47.961 --> 03:41:49.067
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: we know na meron kayong mga tina-transfer

asr-003831
03:41:49.067 --> 03:41:52.388
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: sa mga penal colonies

asr-003832
03:41:52.388 --> 03:41:53.495
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: na mga PDLs.

asr-003833
03:41:53.495 --> 03:41:54.602
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: That's correct.

asr-003834
03:41:54.602 --> 03:41:56.815
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Nababantayan ho ba talaga iyon?

asr-003835
03:41:56.815 --> 03:42:08.703
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ang ginawa ko, for the longest time, iyong Chinese drug lords sa NBP, nilipat ko lahat sa Mindoro, sa Supermax.

asr-003836
03:42:08.880 --> 03:42:17.263
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: At iyong report naman namin, we will submit to you, na drastically nabawasan na natin ang pagpasok ng mga drugs.

asr-003837
03:42:17.263 --> 03:42:29.075
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: May mga nangyayari po. Iyong bibisitang misis may dala-dalang drugs, nilalagay sa private parts.

asr-003838
03:42:30.123 --> 03:42:37.114
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Meron ngang kuwento sa akin iyong mga guard, nagbibiro: nahuli raw nila kasi iyong cellphone nag-ring.

asr-003839
03:42:37.781 --> 03:42:42.811
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: And then nakuha doon sa private parts niya, may cellphone, may adaptor, meron pang drugs.

asr-003840
03:42:43.306 --> 03:42:45.154
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So napakaliit na babae.

asr-003841
03:42:45.345 --> 03:42:45.821
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Opo. Totoo po.

asr-003842
03:42:45.840 --> 03:42:45.954
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Yes, that's true.

asr-003843
03:42:46.202 --> 03:42:46.812
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Paano po iyon?

asr-003844
03:42:47.250 --> 03:42:48.641
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Meron pong nangyaring ganoon.

asr-003845
03:42:49.479 --> 03:42:58.656
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Kaya talaga po, pagka ayaw nilang magpa-inspection, hindi na po namin puwedeng mag-conjugal visit kung ayaw magpa-inspect noong misis.

asr-003846
03:43:01.762 --> 03:43:08.761
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Tinatanong ko rin po iyan kasi iyong mga so-called witnesses doon sa kaso ko, those who gave perjurious testimonies,

asr-003847
03:43:09.467 --> 03:43:12.593
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: iyong mga nai-transfer na po, iyon ho ba iyong mga nababantayan?

asr-003848
03:43:13.602 --> 03:43:14.610
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: They were watched.

asr-003849
03:43:15.034 --> 03:43:15.215
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: That's why.

asr-003850
03:43:15.881 --> 03:43:17.757
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: You know who I’m referring to?

asr-003851
03:43:17.858 --> 03:43:24.110
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: All those drug lords, those witnesses who testified in my cases—they were supposed to be transferred.

asr-003852
03:43:24.473 --> 03:43:25.885
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Nandoon po sila sa Mindoro?

asr-003853
03:43:26.954 --> 03:43:27.398
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes.

asr-003854
03:43:27.640 --> 03:43:29.688
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Pag bumibisita ako, nagno-noise barrage sila.

asr-003855
03:43:30.543 --> 03:43:32.888
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Tapos sabi ko, “Picturan mo lahat iyong nag-iingay.”

asr-003856
03:43:33.127 --> 03:43:38.196
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Hahanapan ko pa ng isang isla iyan. Ilagay ko sa isang isla na separate branch.

asr-003857
03:43:38.196 --> 03:43:40.463
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Kasi nagrereklamo sila.

asr-003858
03:43:41.059 --> 03:43:43.803
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Nagrereklamo po kasi nilipat sila doon sa Mindoro.

asr-003859
03:43:44.399 --> 03:43:45.254
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: So, really...

asr-003860
03:43:45.254 --> 03:43:48.037
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: They would want back to New Bilibid Prison.

asr-003861
03:43:48.037 --> 03:43:52.013
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Sa New Bilibid po, medyo mahirap po talagang ma-secure dahil—

asr-003862
03:43:52.709 --> 03:43:58.275
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: kaya kailangan po isara na po natin iyang New Bilibid Prison dahil napaka-crowded po talaga.

asr-003863
03:43:59.548 --> 03:44:00.045
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: At regional na lang.

asr-003864
03:44:00.840 --> 03:44:01.921
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes.

asr-003865
03:44:04.000 --> 03:44:05.872
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: I have no time anymore.

asr-003866
03:44:05.992 --> 03:44:08.756
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: I have questions supposedly to DOJ proper, but I have no time.

asr-003867
03:44:08.825 --> 03:44:10.817
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Thank you very much, Mr. Chair.

asr-003868
03:44:11.040 --> 03:44:11.404
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Thank you, Cong. Leila.

asr-003869
03:44:11.404 --> 03:44:11.977
Rep. Leila M. de Lima: Maraming salamat po.

asr-003870
03:44:12.914 --> 03:44:13.781
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line...

asr-003871
03:44:13.781 --> 03:44:14.649
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Next in line…

asr-003872
03:44:16.800 --> 03:44:24.790
Rep. Mikaela Angela B. Suansing: Of course, my predecessor, previous sponsor of the DOJ budget, Cong Rufus Rodriguez.

asr-003873
03:44:26.560 --> 03:44:28.096
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-003874
03:44:28.236 --> 03:44:33.404
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Good afternoon to my distinguished colleagues and our valued resource persons this afternoon.

asr-003875
03:44:34.502 --> 03:44:43.740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So I am here because I am here to support the budget of the OSEC and all the departments

asr-003876
03:44:43.740 --> 03:44:47.411
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and attached agencies of the Department of Justice.

asr-003877
03:44:47.411 --> 03:44:47.691
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Why?

asr-003878
03:44:47.711 --> 03:44:47.870
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Why?

asr-003879
03:44:49.267 --> 03:44:58.047
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I finished my undergraduate studies in De La Salle because I was able to get the salary of my father,

asr-003880
03:44:58.905 --> 03:45:02.496
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: who was for 20 years provincial fiscal of Misamis Oriental.

asr-003881
03:45:03.235 --> 03:45:10.917
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And I would go to the, you know, La Salle, and then we go by jeepney to Padre Faura and get it.

asr-003882
03:45:10.917 --> 03:45:12.214
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So thank you again.

asr-003883
03:45:12.832 --> 03:45:17.641
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: My life, therefore, has a history of support from the Department of Justice,

asr-003884
03:45:17.641 --> 03:45:21.073
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and we can never, our family can never forget that.

asr-003885
03:45:21.612 --> 03:45:28.705
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So first questions will be—these questions are leading questions—

asr-003886
03:45:30.142 --> 03:45:32.437
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: To increase the budget of the OSEC.

asr-003887
03:45:32.536 --> 03:45:34.691
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Mr. Secretary, Frederick Vida.

asr-003888
03:45:35.210 --> 03:45:35.669
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes, sir.

asr-003889
03:45:35.689 --> 03:45:38.503
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The OSEC, while it looks like there is an increase,

asr-003890
03:45:39.680 --> 03:45:47.841
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: however, your MOOE has been reduced from 1.9 to only 1.6,

asr-003891
03:45:47.841 --> 03:45:49.138
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: so that 203.

asr-003892
03:45:49.717 --> 03:45:53.767
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: million decrease. What is your wish on this, Mr. Secretary?

asr-003893
03:45:58.117 --> 03:46:04.801
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Your Honor, to meet the levels of 2026, to be restored to that level,

asr-003894
03:46:05.280 --> 03:46:11.945
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: so that the department would have sufficient resources to fulfill its mandate, Your Honor.

asr-003895
03:46:12.683 --> 03:46:13.142
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-003896
03:46:13.142 --> 03:46:17.951
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So we will work on that in the BARC, in our Committee of Vice Chairpersons,

asr-003897
03:46:18.370 --> 03:46:20.764
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and then hopefully in the BICAM.

asr-003898
03:46:21.263 --> 03:46:21.961
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So thank you.

asr-003899
03:46:21.961 --> 03:46:23.358
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So restoration of 2.9.

asr-003900
03:46:23.358 --> 03:46:26.291
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 2.3 for Secretary of Justice Vida.

asr-003901
03:46:26.391 --> 03:46:26.930
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Is that all?

asr-003902
03:46:31.200 --> 03:46:32.382
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Of course, Your Honor.

asr-003903
03:46:32.802 --> 03:46:35.847
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: We made mention earlier of the request,

asr-003904
03:46:36.087 --> 03:46:41.375
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: so particularly on the reduction of the NEP 2027

asr-003905
03:46:41.375 --> 03:46:45.321
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: from the proposed budget for the Office of the Cybercrime,

asr-003906
03:46:45.902 --> 03:46:49.808
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: the NCC-OSAEC and the IACAT.

asr-003907
03:46:50.249 --> 03:46:52.052
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Those are of particular importance,

asr-003908
03:46:52.693 --> 03:46:56.819
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: which we do not want to lose the momentum that we have now, Your Honor.

asr-003909
03:46:57.059 --> 03:46:59.102
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much for the three agencies?

asr-003910
03:47:00.164 --> 03:47:04.030
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Similarly, Your Honor, to be restored to the levels of 2026.

asr-003911
03:47:04.330 --> 03:47:04.771
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Which is?

asr-003912
03:47:05.352 --> 03:47:06.153
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Which is?

asr-003913
03:47:07.475 --> 03:47:09.839
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Take note, because we're going to work for this.

asr-003914
03:47:12.893 --> 03:47:14.095
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Forty-five, seventy.

asr-003915
03:47:18.862 --> 03:47:20.865
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Approximately 130 million, Your Honor.

asr-003916
03:47:21.787 --> 03:47:22.027
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Only?

asr-003917
03:47:22.528 --> 03:47:24.130
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For the three agencies?

asr-003918
03:47:24.351 --> 03:47:25.012
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes, for...

asr-003919
03:47:25.693 --> 03:47:28.717
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please, please note down, because we’re going to make sure that it will be restored.

asr-003920
03:47:28.717 --> 03:47:29.558
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: To meet the 2026 level.

asr-003921
03:47:29.558 --> 03:47:31.782
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, at least 2026 level.

asr-003922
03:47:32.263 --> 03:47:33.424
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Anything else, Secretary?

asr-003923
03:47:35.618 --> 03:47:41.587
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Of course, particular interest would be on the request of the NBI

asr-003924
03:47:41.587 --> 03:47:49.839
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: on their pursuit and in the particular challenge in addressing cybercrime

asr-003925
03:47:49.839 --> 03:47:56.109
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: in pursuit of their investigation and their push

asr-003926
03:47:56.109 --> 03:48:03.660
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: so that the requested budget from the DBM be restored on the ICT projects and programs.

asr-003927
03:48:03.720 --> 03:48:04.722
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-003928
03:48:04.722 --> 03:48:08.167
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, good that you've mentioned, because I'm going to go one by one,

asr-003929
03:48:08.648 --> 03:48:12.393
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: those who were reduced in their 2027 NEP.

asr-003930
03:48:12.934 --> 03:48:15.418
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we're going now to NBI, because mentioned already.

asr-003931
03:48:16.800 --> 03:48:20.391
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Director Melvin Matibag,

asr-003932
03:48:20.950 --> 03:48:24.501
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: is it correct that your agency,

asr-003933
03:48:25.239 --> 03:48:27.294
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: the National Bureau of Investigation,

asr-003934
03:48:27.294 --> 03:48:30.346
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: from 3.791 million,

asr-003935
03:48:31.024 --> 03:48:33.518
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: it is now only 2.9 billion?

asr-003936
03:48:33.578 --> 03:48:33.678
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: All right.

asr-003937
03:48:33.698 --> 03:48:39.663
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It’s a decrease of 882 million, 23.2 percent.

asr-003938
03:48:39.742 --> 03:48:40.381
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Is that correct?

asr-003939
03:48:41.059 --> 03:48:41.777
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Yes, sir.

asr-003940
03:48:42.176 --> 03:48:42.875
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-003941
03:48:43.114 --> 03:48:44.291
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How can they do that to you?

asr-003942
03:48:45.767 --> 03:48:46.825
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: I have no idea.

asr-003943
03:48:47.363 --> 03:48:52.231
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Just to be clear, I think the reason why is the utilization at that time,

asr-003944
03:48:52.610 --> 03:48:57.159
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: because there are some ICT projects that need to be aligned,

asr-003945
03:48:58.017 --> 03:48:58.475
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: be completed.

asr-003946
03:48:58.475 --> 03:49:03.603
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: But right now, we have recognized the reasons for that,

asr-003947
03:49:03.622 --> 03:49:05.617
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: and I think the...

asr-003948
03:49:06.356 --> 03:49:07.333
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The catch-up plan, right?

asr-003949
03:49:07.553 --> 03:49:08.211
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: That's correct.

asr-003950
03:49:08.311 --> 03:49:10.445
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So you finish everything by December 31?

asr-003951
03:49:10.525 --> 03:49:13.418
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: By December, we will have 98 percent utilization.

asr-003952
03:49:13.677 --> 03:49:19.343
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: The remaining 2 percent will be for the maintenance of the ICT that we will be installing,

asr-003953
03:49:19.483 --> 03:49:22.096
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: which has already been obligated by this time, Your Honor.

asr-003954
03:49:22.734 --> 03:49:23.253
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Very good.

asr-003955
03:49:23.373 --> 03:49:26.744
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So assuming, because we will assume that you will do it.

asr-003956
03:49:26.784 --> 03:49:27.902
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You’re a very good director.

asr-003957
03:49:28.261 --> 03:49:28.580
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Thank you.

asr-003958
03:49:28.580 --> 03:49:30.874
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So you will be able...

asr-003959
03:49:30.874 --> 03:49:33.507
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Can you place here a restoration of 880?

asr-003960
03:49:33.547 --> 03:49:35.762
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 882 million, correct?

asr-003961
03:49:36.201 --> 03:49:36.679
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Yes.

asr-003962
03:49:36.819 --> 03:49:37.916
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And you're satisfied with that?

asr-003963
03:49:38.176 --> 03:49:41.846
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Well, I have a specific request, Mr. Chair.

asr-003964
03:49:42.186 --> 03:49:43.223
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Say that now.

asr-003965
03:49:43.702 --> 03:49:45.338
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It will not be counted against my time.

asr-003966
03:49:45.457 --> 03:49:52.101
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Our agents right now is getting a hazard pay of only 4,000 pesos monthly.

asr-003967
03:49:52.739 --> 03:49:57.108
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: So we are requesting at least we can be leveled with the other law enforcements,

asr-003968
03:49:57.108 --> 03:50:03.452
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: which is probably the reasonable amount will be 15,000 monthly for them to operate properly,

asr-003969
03:50:03.472 --> 03:50:07.123
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: our agents has been transferred from one province to another,

asr-003970
03:50:07.123 --> 03:50:12.250
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: and they’ve been operating 24/7, like the concern on the issue of OSAEC.

asr-003971
03:50:13.188 --> 03:50:17.776
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Records will reveal that we have so many operations and apprehensions on OSAEC

asr-003972
03:50:17.776 --> 03:50:22.245
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: and other crimes, cyber crimes also, which we've been addressing.

asr-003973
03:50:23.063 --> 03:50:30.444
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: So I'm respectfully requesting that the hazard pay of our agents from 4,000 be increased to 15,000 at least.

asr-003974
03:50:30.784 --> 03:50:31.482
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 15,000?

asr-003975
03:50:31.641 --> 03:50:31.881
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Yes.

asr-003976
03:50:32.160 --> 03:50:32.579
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Approved.

asr-003977
03:50:32.579 --> 03:50:33.377
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Thank you.

asr-003978
03:50:33.397 --> 03:50:34.375
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: From me, from me.

asr-003979
03:50:35.232 --> 03:50:35.352
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-003980
03:50:37.367 --> 03:50:38.225
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Work for that.

asr-003981
03:50:38.464 --> 03:50:39.043
NBI Director Melvin Matibag: Salamat po.

asr-003982
03:50:40.200 --> 03:50:45.446
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: The NBI director is my good, you know, our cherished faculty member.

asr-003983
03:50:45.585 --> 03:50:51.529
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I was dean of San Sebastian College of Law, and I personally requested President Rueda to teach,

asr-003984
03:50:51.869 --> 03:50:53.903
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: and he was there for quite some time with me.

asr-003985
03:50:54.422 --> 03:50:58.072
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And so now to Chief Rueda-Acosta, what do you need?

asr-003986
03:50:58.072 --> 03:51:02.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I think it will be about the opening of more, you know,

asr-003987
03:51:02.939 --> 03:51:03.238
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: PAO.

asr-003988
03:51:03.318 --> 03:51:11.994
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: PAO lawyers because of the ratio of courts vis-a-vis the PAO attorneys.

asr-003989
03:51:12.912 --> 03:51:15.984
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: We need 559 lawyers, Your Honor.

asr-003990
03:51:16.343 --> 03:51:18.377
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: We are amenable to half the number.

asr-003991
03:51:18.776 --> 03:51:20.372
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is 500?

asr-003992
03:51:20.950 --> 03:51:21.808
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Yes, 500.

asr-003993
03:51:22.027 --> 03:51:23.084
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is that?

asr-003994
03:51:23.603 --> 03:51:24.860
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: One billion, Your Honor.

asr-003995
03:51:25.538 --> 03:51:26.794
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You just know it.

asr-003996
03:51:27.393 --> 03:51:28.989
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Because of the high salary.

asr-003997
03:51:30.125 --> 03:51:31.741
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: We are amenable to half.

asr-003998
03:51:31.741 --> 03:51:32.958
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is one half?

asr-003999
03:51:33.237 --> 03:51:35.531
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Half, only, Your Honor.

asr-004000
03:51:35.671 --> 03:51:37.924
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Maybe 225 new lawyers.

asr-004001
03:51:38.463 --> 03:51:40.158
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: But give us 400 staff.

asr-004002
03:51:40.258 --> 03:51:41.216
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: We have no staff.

asr-004003
03:51:42.093 --> 03:51:43.948
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: There is no creation of staff position.

asr-004004
03:51:44.148 --> 03:51:46.402
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much will be the total of that?

asr-004005
03:51:46.820 --> 03:51:49.792
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Meaning both the PAO lawyers and the staff?

asr-004006
03:51:50.471 --> 03:51:53.722
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: 200 lawyers, maybe, and 400 staff.

asr-004007
03:51:53.842 --> 03:51:56.355
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: That may be around 600 million.

asr-004008
03:51:57.093 --> 03:51:57.691
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Reasonable?

asr-004009
03:51:58.948 --> 03:52:00.583
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Around 700 million.

asr-004010
03:52:00.623 --> 03:52:01.561
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Oh, reasonable also.

asr-004011
03:52:01.561 --> 03:52:02.897
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So 700.

asr-004012
03:52:03.156 --> 03:52:04.154
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: 700 million.

asr-004013
03:52:04.154 --> 03:52:05.151
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We try to have that.

asr-004014
03:52:05.151 --> 03:52:06.148
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004015
03:52:06.148 --> 03:52:09.140
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because the Department of Justice and our PAO should support it.

asr-004016
03:52:09.140 --> 03:52:10.138
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004017
03:52:10.138 --> 03:52:11.135
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Thank you, Your Honor.

asr-004018
03:52:11.135 --> 03:52:12.132
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Remember, I worked hard for this last year.

asr-004019
03:52:12.132 --> 03:52:13.130
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004020
03:52:13.130 --> 03:52:14.127
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: They knew.

asr-004021
03:52:14.127 --> 03:52:15.124
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But fortunately, there was no...

asr-004022
03:52:15.124 --> 03:52:18.116
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: There is continuous creation of courts, branches of courts.

asr-004023
03:52:18.116 --> 03:52:19.113
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: That's correct.

asr-004024
03:52:19.113 --> 03:52:20.111
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: That's correct.

asr-004025
03:52:20.111 --> 03:52:23.103
PAO Chief Persida V. Rueda-Acosta: So we need fiscals and PAO lawyers at the same time, Your Honor.

asr-004026
03:52:23.103 --> 03:52:24.100
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-004027
03:52:24.100 --> 03:52:30.565
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then, of course, my favorite, Commissioner of the Bureau of Immigration, where I was once

asr-004028
03:52:30.565 --> 03:52:31.556
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: one of the Bureau.

asr-004029
03:52:31.556 --> 03:52:32.548
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's correct.

asr-004030
03:52:32.548 --> 03:52:41.471
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Commissioner, I understand here in your office, the BI has been greatly reduced by

asr-004031
03:52:41.471 --> 03:52:44.446
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 1.6 billion.

asr-004032
03:52:44.446 --> 03:52:49.404
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How is that, Commissioner Viado, with your very outstanding performance there?

asr-004033
03:52:49.404 --> 03:52:50.395
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You're doing so well.

asr-004034
03:52:50.395 --> 03:52:52.378
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Why are they reducing that?

asr-004035
03:52:52.378 --> 03:52:55.353
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: I don't know the reason why, Your Honor.

asr-004036
03:52:55.353 --> 03:52:57.336
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But thank you very much for the endorsement.

asr-004037
03:52:57.336 --> 03:53:01.302
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And we will increase the additional budget.

asr-004038
03:53:01.302 --> 03:53:02.293
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yeah.

asr-004039
03:53:02.293 --> 03:53:07.251
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What will be the more important priority budget you would request from the committee?

asr-004040
03:53:07.251 --> 03:53:09.234
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thank you very much, Your Honor.

asr-004041
03:53:09.234 --> 03:53:16.175
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: First and foremost, we would like to inform the committee and, of course, the honorable

asr-004042
03:53:16.175 --> 03:53:22.124
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Representative, Congressman Rodriguez, that we already moved to our new building, Your

asr-004043
03:53:22.124 --> 03:53:23.115
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Honor.

asr-004044
03:53:23.115 --> 03:53:24.107
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So we would...

asr-004045
03:53:24.107 --> 03:53:25.098
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004046
03:53:25.098 --> 03:53:30.056
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And we would need the budget for capital outlay for the post-construction of the new BI building.

asr-004047
03:53:30.056 --> 03:53:31.047
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It was removed, Your Honor.

asr-004048
03:53:31.047 --> 03:53:32.039
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is that?

asr-004049
03:53:32.039 --> 03:53:33.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: In the amount of 276,280,000, Your Honor.

asr-004050
03:53:33.030 --> 03:53:34.022
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-004051
03:53:34.022 --> 03:53:35.013
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What else?

asr-004052
03:53:35.013 --> 03:53:45.920
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And we would also like to ask for the capital outlay for the locally funded projects for

asr-004053
03:53:45.920 --> 03:53:50.878
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: the development, enhancement, and procurement of IT systems and infrastructures, not only

asr-004054
03:53:50.878 --> 03:53:56.827
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: within the main building, the new BI building, but also our support offices, Your Honor.

asr-004055
03:53:56.827 --> 03:53:57.818
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So the amount is...

asr-004056
03:53:57.818 --> 03:53:58.810
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Total is 1,200,527,811, Your Honor.

asr-004057
03:53:58.810 --> 03:53:59.801
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-004058
03:53:59.801 --> 03:54:00.793
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: 527,811, Your Honor.

asr-004059
03:54:00.793 --> 03:54:01.784
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Of that for you to be able to perform.

asr-004060
03:54:01.784 --> 03:54:02.776
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004061
03:54:02.776 --> 03:54:03.767
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And I was in your new building with Secretary Rimulya at the time.

asr-004062
03:54:03.767 --> 03:54:04.759
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004063
03:54:04.759 --> 03:54:05.751
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And it’s a very good building right there on Macapagal Avenue.

asr-004064
03:54:05.751 --> 03:54:06.742
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004065
03:54:06.742 --> 03:54:07.734
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-004066
03:54:07.734 --> 03:54:08.725
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Anything else?

asr-004067
03:54:08.725 --> 03:54:09.717
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's all, Your Honor.

asr-004068
03:54:09.717 --> 03:54:10.708
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Thank you very much.

asr-004069
03:54:10.708 --> 03:54:11.700
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much.

asr-004070
03:54:11.700 --> 03:54:12.691
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-004071
03:54:12.691 --> 03:54:13.683
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: We will work on this.

asr-004072
03:54:13.683 --> 03:54:14.674
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-004073
03:54:14.674 --> 03:54:15.666
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then next, we will have the OSG.

asr-004074
03:54:15.666 --> 03:54:16.657
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Solicitor General Darlene Marie Berberabe is here.

asr-004075
03:54:16.657 --> 03:54:17.649
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004089
03:54:31.530 --> 03:54:32.531
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You have an increase, but do you need more?

asr-004090
03:54:32.531 --> 03:54:33.531
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004091
03:54:33.531 --> 03:54:47.740
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: The increase of 248 million, I think 255 will go to the first-year installment for the building

asr-004092
03:54:47.740 --> 03:54:58.227
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: that OSG will procure through the GSIS lease-to-own financing framework.

asr-004093
03:54:58.227 --> 03:54:59.228
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: So . . .

asr-004094
03:54:59.228 --> 03:55:03.230
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Iyon po iyong nasa ISSP, 123 million.

asr-004095
03:55:03.830 --> 03:55:07.873
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How much is the entire building? Because the Ombudsman is buying, GSIS also.

asr-004096
03:55:08.113 --> 03:55:14.237
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Yung sa OSG po, total of 4.5 billion pesos for the whole OSG,

asr-004097
03:55:15.118 --> 03:55:17.879
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: and may balik din po naman sa government,

asr-004098
03:55:18.039 --> 03:55:22.482
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: sapagkat ibebenta po yung OSG main building now sa Amor Solo Street,

asr-004099
03:55:22.622 --> 03:55:23.723
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: so babalik po yun.

asr-004100
03:55:24.043 --> 03:55:27.966
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: So around maybe 800 million to 1 billion pesos din po yun.

asr-004101
03:55:27.966 --> 03:55:31.908
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: And then, ang hiningi lang po namin ay dahil through the MYCA,

asr-004102
03:55:32.469 --> 03:55:38.933
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: so 255 million will go to the first year installment to be paid to GSIS.

asr-004103
03:55:39.053 --> 03:55:39.913
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: 250 million?

asr-004104
03:55:40.994 --> 03:55:41.714
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: First year?

asr-004105
03:55:42.035 --> 03:55:44.356
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: First year. So iyon po iyong nakalagay sa NEP.

asr-004106
03:55:44.736 --> 03:55:47.538
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Has the DBM approved your MYCA proposal?

asr-004107
03:55:47.718 --> 03:55:52.441
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because if it is there, every year we'll be able to put a budget.

asr-004108
03:55:52.441 --> 03:55:57.805
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Yes, ang nailagay po ng DBM dahil ang timeline po namin,

asr-004109
03:55:57.985 --> 03:56:02.868
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: six months pa to kung makonfirm, then mafifit out po yung building.

asr-004110
03:56:03.128 --> 03:56:04.669
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: So half year lang po.

asr-004111
03:56:05.790 --> 03:56:12.734
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Ang nawala po yung sa computerization, sa digital transformation program po yung 100 million.

asr-004112
03:56:12.734 --> 03:56:14.235
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Very important. How much is that?

asr-004113
03:56:14.875 --> 03:56:16.256
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: 123 million po.

asr-004114
03:56:16.757 --> 03:56:18.738
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Computerization, we need that very much.

asr-004115
03:56:18.758 --> 03:56:19.058
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Yes.

asr-004116
03:56:19.298 --> 03:56:22.220
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Plus the building, 250 for the year, next year.

asr-004117
03:56:22.220 --> 03:56:25.202
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Iyong pong building, nandoon na po iyon sa NEP.

asr-004118
03:56:25.582 --> 03:56:27.223
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: So ang medyo inihihirit po yung...

asr-004119
03:56:28.004 --> 03:56:31.546
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: na-exclude po, gawa ng isiningit po yung sa building.

asr-004120
03:56:31.686 --> 03:56:34.608
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay. Digitalization is very important.

asr-004121
03:56:34.768 --> 03:56:35.088
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Thank you.

asr-004122
03:56:35.448 --> 03:56:36.649
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So anything else?

asr-004123
03:56:37.610 --> 03:56:43.553
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Our solicitor general, who is doing a very good job in the Supreme Court of the Republic of the Philippines.

asr-004124
03:56:44.114 --> 03:56:45.335
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Thank you. Thank you po.

asr-004125
03:56:45.335 --> 03:56:51.939
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Na-iraos na po natin ang GAA oral argument sa Supreme Court.

asr-004126
03:56:52.019 --> 03:56:53.720
Solicitor General Darlene Marie B. Berberabe: Thank you, Congressman Rufus.

asr-004127
03:56:53.900 --> 03:56:57.781
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And we have the office of the ADR reduced also.

asr-004128
03:56:58.022 --> 03:57:01.963
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Very small part, reduced pa. Where is the OADR head?

asr-004129
03:57:02.723 --> 03:57:05.244
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Here, sir. Good afternoon, sir.

asr-004130
03:57:06.265 --> 03:57:06.725
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Here.

asr-004131
03:57:07.625 --> 03:57:08.245
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yes, sir.

asr-004132
03:57:08.805 --> 03:57:11.967
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It was reduced by 26 million.

asr-004133
03:57:12.547 --> 03:57:13.167
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: That's right.

asr-004134
03:57:14.748 --> 03:57:15.908
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What is your wish?

asr-004135
03:57:16.088 --> 03:57:24.351
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Well, you are like some other official saying, I just scolded the CDA representative in that hearing just recently

asr-004136
03:57:24.351 --> 03:57:27.913
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: with the Department of Industry.

asr-004137
03:57:28.033 --> 03:57:32.714
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because he said, he said, this budget will do.

asr-004138
03:57:32.854 --> 03:57:33.735
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Can you imagine that?

asr-004139
03:57:35.475 --> 03:57:37.296
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: He will agree to the small budget.

asr-004140
03:57:37.836 --> 03:57:41.718
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: He will never say that in a budget hearing that we will make do with the budget.

asr-004141
03:57:42.198 --> 03:57:46.579
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You fight always so that you will have an increase in your budget.

asr-004142
03:57:46.739 --> 03:57:47.420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What do you say?

asr-004143
03:57:48.300 --> 03:57:49.540
OADR Executive Director Jose Maria Palaganas: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-004144
03:57:49.540 --> 03:57:50.021
OADR Executive Director Jose Maria Palaganas: Rufus.

asr-004145
03:57:50.021 --> 03:57:58.004
OADR Executive Director Jose Maria Palaganas: We would like to propose restoring it to the original 168 million for 2027.

asr-004146
03:57:58.044 --> 03:58:03.506
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So we restore 26 million, correct?

asr-004147
03:58:04.206 --> 03:58:04.666
OADR Executive Director Jose Maria Palaganas: That's right.

asr-004148
03:58:04.666 --> 03:58:05.366
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: OADR, right?

asr-004149
03:58:05.506 --> 03:58:05.826
OADR Executive Director Jose Maria Palaganas: That's right.

asr-004150
03:58:06.407 --> 03:58:08.988
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Oh, OGCC also reduced.

asr-004151
03:58:09.748 --> 03:58:11.489
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Please say your piece.

asr-004152
03:58:15.900 --> 03:58:23.723
Office of the Government Corporate Counsel representative: Mr. Chairman, we will defer to the judgment of the DBM, Your Honor.

asr-004153
03:58:23.743 --> 03:58:25.204
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You never defer to the judgment.

asr-004154
03:58:25.364 --> 03:58:26.384
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: They always lower everything.

asr-004155
03:58:27.945 --> 03:58:29.665
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Anyway, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004156
03:58:29.685 --> 03:58:40.069
Office of the Government Corporate Counsel representative: Mr. Chairman, we have an optimization plan that we presented to the DBM and we hope they will...

asr-004157
03:58:40.069 --> 03:58:42.710
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, we will work also for you.

asr-004158
03:58:43.290 --> 03:58:50.773
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And then, my second-to-the-last question is the Parole and Probation Administration.

asr-004159
03:58:50.873 --> 03:58:51.433
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: My goodness.

asr-004160
03:58:52.194 --> 03:58:53.154
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Your budget is small.

asr-004161
03:58:53.854 --> 03:58:57.075
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Reduced by 49 million.

asr-004162
03:58:57.195 --> 03:58:57.916
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: What can you say?

asr-004163
03:58:58.396 --> 03:58:59.656
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Administrator Benitez,

asr-004164
03:58:59.696 --> 03:59:00.176
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Where are you?

asr-004165
03:59:05.098 --> 03:59:05.458
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ah, yes.

asr-004166
03:59:07.099 --> 03:59:07.939
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: For...

asr-004167
03:59:07.939 --> 03:59:08.580
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Bukor.

asr-004168
03:59:08.780 --> 03:59:09.260
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Ah, Bukor.

asr-004169
03:59:09.400 --> 03:59:10.640
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Bukor, let me see.

asr-004170
03:59:12.841 --> 03:59:14.242
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Ah, you were increased.

asr-004171
03:59:14.942 --> 03:59:17.323
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So, are you thanking the DBM for that?

asr-004172
03:59:17.863 --> 03:59:23.405
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: We are requesting more for next year.

asr-004173
03:59:23.525 --> 03:59:27.106
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: But hopefully, this budget will not anymore be touched.

asr-004174
03:59:27.807 --> 03:59:30.148
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: It will never be reduced, but it will be increased.

asr-004175
03:59:30.648 --> 03:59:32.168
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes, thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004176
03:59:32.168 --> 03:59:32.969
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How about the...

asr-004177
03:59:33.809 --> 03:59:34.909
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Administrator Benitez.

asr-004178
03:59:35.910 --> 03:59:36.850
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Ah, you are Administrator Benitez.

asr-004179
03:59:36.850 --> 03:59:37.785
BuCor Director General Gregorio Pio P. Catapang Jr.: Yes, sir.

asr-004180
03:59:37.785 --> 03:59:39.676
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: How about the Parole and Probation Administration?

asr-004181
03:59:39.676 --> 03:59:40.671
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Your Honor.

asr-004182
03:59:40.671 --> 03:59:41.667
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Sino?

asr-004183
03:59:41.667 --> 03:59:42.841
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Parole Probation?

asr-004184
03:59:42.841 --> 03:59:43.836
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yeah.

asr-004185
03:59:43.836 --> 03:59:45.249
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: You are General?

asr-004186
03:59:45.249 --> 03:59:46.662
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Bienvenido, sir.

asr-004187
03:59:47.100 --> 03:59:47.500
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Yes, sir.

asr-004188
03:59:48.120 --> 03:59:50.280
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So I have a wrong addressee.

asr-004189
03:59:50.940 --> 03:59:53.500
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So I have some letter for you.

asr-004190
03:59:54.200 --> 04:00:00.080
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So the parole probation, again, was reduced by 49 million.

asr-004191
04:00:00.840 --> 04:00:01.300
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004192
04:00:01.300 --> 04:00:03.260
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So what are the important items to be restored?

asr-004193
04:00:04.840 --> 04:00:08.880
Parole and Probation Administration representative: In our case, we were reduced by 49 million,

asr-004194
04:00:08.880 --> 04:00:14.160
Parole and Probation Administration representative: pero po kasi intact na po kami sa ISSP computerization namin.

asr-004195
04:00:14.160 --> 04:00:20.080
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Ang wish list po namin ay para sa probation officers’ ladderized

asr-004196
04:00:20.320 --> 04:00:26.160
Parole and Probation Administration representative: three-year improvement program for their major competencies po.

asr-004197
04:00:26.420 --> 04:00:34.080
Parole and Probation Administration representative: This is about 8,198,000 for a three-year period.

asr-004198
04:00:36.100 --> 04:00:37.860
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Eight million?

asr-004199
04:00:38.100 --> 04:00:39.180
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So not billion?

asr-004200
04:00:39.700 --> 04:00:40.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Very small?

asr-004201
04:00:41.120 --> 04:00:41.540
Parole and Probation Administration representative: Yes, sir.

asr-004202
04:00:41.540 --> 04:00:42.440
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Eight million.

asr-004203
04:00:42.660 --> 04:00:43.880
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So we'll try to work on that.

asr-004204
04:00:44.160 --> 04:00:45.440
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Any other agency not called?

asr-004205
04:00:45.540 --> 04:00:47.540
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Because I think I called everybody already.

asr-004206
04:00:51.340 --> 04:00:52.900
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I'll just, okay.

asr-004207
04:00:53.520 --> 04:00:54.920
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Lahat naman yata nakuha na, no?

asr-004208
04:00:55.820 --> 04:00:57.420
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: PCGG, yes?

asr-004209
04:00:57.960 --> 04:00:58.480
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: PCGG.

asr-004210
04:00:59.040 --> 04:00:59.300
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Yeah.

asr-004211
04:01:00.060 --> 04:01:01.600
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Well, you have an increase here.

asr-004212
04:01:02.120 --> 04:01:03.740
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: But what is the wish of PCGG?

asr-004213
04:01:03.740 --> 04:01:13.820
PCGG Chairperson: Ang wish po namin, eto talagang wish po, is more institutional rather than budgetary.

asr-004214
04:01:14.380 --> 04:01:14.800
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Okay.

asr-004215
04:01:14.800 --> 04:01:14.860
PCGG Chairperson: Okay.

asr-004216
04:01:15.440 --> 04:01:22.960
PCGG Chairperson: So our wish is that the mandate of the PCGG will be expanded, but this requires a law po kasi.

asr-004217
04:01:22.960 --> 04:01:27.400
PCGG Chairperson: Because presently po, our mandate is limited.

asr-004218
04:01:28.080 --> 04:01:31.640
PCGG Chairperson: It's limited to a few individuals only.

asr-004219
04:01:32.620 --> 04:01:41.840
PCGG Chairperson: And so we would like to expand sana yung mandate ng PCGG to include all public officials.

asr-004220
04:01:43.600 --> 04:01:44.980
PCGG Chairperson: Right now po,

asr-004221
04:01:45.440 --> 04:01:49.780
PCGG Chairperson: Mandate namin is to file civil forfeiture cases.

asr-004222
04:01:50.360 --> 04:01:58.680
PCGG Chairperson: So as far as corruption is concerned, that is the template that has been used by the PCGG for the past 40 years.

asr-004223
04:01:58.680 --> 04:02:05.020
PCGG Chairperson: And we were able to recover more than 300 billion only through civil forfeiture.

asr-004224
04:02:05.700 --> 04:02:10.340
PCGG Chairperson: Wala po kaming naipakulong, pero we were able to recover that much.

asr-004225
04:02:10.900 --> 04:02:14.360
PCGG Chairperson: And so gusto po sana namin ma-expand yung mandate.

asr-004226
04:02:14.360 --> 04:02:19.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Perhaps we can now give way to a new mandate.

asr-004227
04:02:19.280 --> 04:02:21.400
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I understand there's already a bill for that.

asr-004228
04:02:21.660 --> 04:02:22.140
PCGG Chairperson: Yes po.

asr-004229
04:02:22.320 --> 04:02:23.660
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: So I will be a co-author.

asr-004230
04:02:24.420 --> 04:02:24.820
PCGG Chairperson: Yes po.

asr-004231
04:02:24.820 --> 04:02:30.380
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For that, so that you will be able to expand your powers.

asr-004232
04:02:30.660 --> 04:02:34.800
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: With that, Mr. Chairman, I thank you for being lenient with me.

asr-004233
04:02:34.800 --> 04:02:40.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: I congratulate Secretary Vida for an outstanding performance as Secretary of Justice.

asr-004234
04:02:41.360 --> 04:02:43.720
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: And all of our attached agencies.

asr-004235
04:02:43.720 --> 04:02:46.580
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Again, you have our support here in Congress.

asr-004236
04:02:46.580 --> 04:02:54.120
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: For after all, justice is an important component of a democracy and development of our nation.

asr-004237
04:02:54.420 --> 04:02:57.620
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you very much, Mr. Chairman, for your leniency in my time.

asr-004238
04:02:57.700 --> 04:02:58.000
Rep. Rufus B. Rodriguez: Thank you.

asr-004239
04:02:58.319 --> 04:02:59.349
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Thank you, Kong Rufus.

asr-004240
04:02:59.359 --> 04:03:10.750
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Thank you for emphasizing the needs of the DOJ and its attached agencies

asr-004241
04:03:10.760 --> 04:03:16.870
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: para po mas maganda pa po yung operations na magawa po nila.

asr-004242
04:03:16.880 --> 04:03:17.910
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Next in line from the minority.

asr-004243
04:03:17.920 --> 04:03:22.990
Rep. Keith Micah "Atty. Mike" D.L. Tan: Representative Egay Erice.

asr-004244
04:03:23.000 --> 04:03:24.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Thank you, Mr. Chairman.

asr-004245
04:03:24.439 --> 04:03:29.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Good afternoon, Secretary Vida and the DOJ family.

asr-004246
04:03:29.520 --> 04:03:36.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: We in the minority strongly supports the promises of Congressman Rufus.

asr-004247
04:03:36.199 --> 04:03:46.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And I think we can assure fiscal space by reducing the appropriations of the House of Representatives.

asr-004248
04:03:46.479 --> 04:03:54.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Anyway.

asr-004256
04:03:54.560 --> 04:03:58.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ang first question ko po, Secretary, para po sa ating immigration.

asr-004257
04:03:58.560 --> 04:04:04.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And this is about the CAIS, the Civil Aviation Immigration Security Services Project.

asr-004258
04:04:04.040 --> 04:04:04.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Good afternoon, Your Honor.

asr-004259
04:04:04.920 --> 04:04:10.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: I would like to maybe appraise of what's the status of the project na.

asr-004260
04:04:10.640 --> 04:04:14.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The current status, Your Honor, po, it is under contract review.

asr-004261
04:04:14.680 --> 04:04:22.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And the final screening will be made by the Department of Finance, the OSG, and the PPP Center, po, Your Honor.

asr-004262
04:04:22.960 --> 04:04:24.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But the contract was already signed?

asr-004263
04:04:24.720 --> 04:04:28.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: No contract has been signed, Your Honor.

asr-004264
04:04:28.199 --> 04:04:38.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So can you just brief us on what's in particular is the contract?

asr-004265
04:04:38.720 --> 04:04:45.670
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: This is a build, train, maintain, transfer modality?

asr-004266
04:04:45.680 --> 04:04:47.389
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's correct, Your Honor.

asr-004267
04:04:47.399 --> 04:04:52.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Build, train, maintain, and transfer modality, it is a public-private partnership proposed

asr-004268
04:04:52.640 --> 04:04:58.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: by SIGRIPORT and delivers an integrated aviation and border security platform.

asr-004269
04:04:58.960 --> 04:05:02.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Combining biometrics, merong advanced analytics.

asr-004270
04:05:02.319 --> 04:05:08.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: When you say, Your Honor, advanced analytics, kahit po yung behavior ng isang tao at the

asr-004271
04:05:08.239 --> 04:05:17.550
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: point wherein kinukuha yung information regarding him, any nervous stick, any facial contortion

asr-004272
04:05:17.560 --> 04:05:24.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: can be read by the system to determine kung high risk po siya at malaking probability

asr-004273
04:05:24.600 --> 04:05:28.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: that he will cause havoc when entering the Philippines.

asr-004274
04:05:28.960 --> 04:05:36.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And it also integrates passenger information systems with the ultimate objective of enhancing

asr-004275
04:05:36.439 --> 04:05:38.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: national security and immigration control.

asr-004276
04:05:39.000 --> 04:05:47.070
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The features of this program include access to billions of facial images.

asr-004277
04:05:47.080 --> 04:05:53.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yung categorization po and then risk scoring, meaning kaya po na nabanggit ko kanina, kung

asr-004278
04:05:54.000 --> 04:06:00.389
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: high risk po yung pasahero na lagi intend na pumasok ng Pilipinas, then ma-analyze po

asr-004279
04:06:00.399 --> 04:06:05.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: at mabibigyan po ng proper tool ang aming immigration officer to decide whether or not

asr-004280
04:06:05.920 --> 04:06:08.110
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: to allow this person to enter.

asr-004281
04:06:08.120 --> 04:06:13.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Meron din pong biographic comparison against criminal and sanctions databases, meaning

asr-004282
04:06:13.880 --> 04:06:17.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: ang interpol po, may access po tayo dyan sa kanilang...

asr-004283
04:06:17.239 --> 04:06:24.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: system, not only sa Central, but all 194 countries sa konektado po sa Interpol.

asr-004284
04:06:24.680 --> 04:06:32.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Meron din pong deception detection analytics based on mga nabanggit ko po, involuntary

asr-004285
04:06:32.159 --> 04:06:33.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: and physical cues.

asr-004286
04:06:34.000 --> 04:06:41.110
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And nandyan din po ang AI-assisted open source intelligence, meaning kung nagkataon po na

asr-004287
04:06:41.120 --> 04:06:47.070
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: let's say 15, 20 years ago, on Facebook, meron po kayong nasabi, which would

asr-004288
04:06:47.080 --> 04:06:54.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: be the system would read as amounting to or gearing towards terrorism.

asr-004289
04:06:54.239 --> 04:06:56.349
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Mababasa rin po yan, Your Honor.

asr-004290
04:06:56.359 --> 04:07:04.750
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang target po nito, Your Honor, is to increase, expand the borders, meaning hindi na lang po

asr-004291
04:07:04.760 --> 04:07:09.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: border natin o physical border po ng Pilipinas ang babantayan.

asr-004292
04:07:09.040 --> 04:07:11.110
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Na-expand po natin yan pagating sa ibang bansa.

asr-004293
04:07:11.120 --> 04:07:17.550
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ngayon po, kung ang isang pasahero nagsusubok pumunta ng Pilipinas, based po sa...

asr-004294
04:07:17.560 --> 04:07:23.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: pagkuhan niya ng ticket, pagkuhan niya ng kanyang passenger reference number, mariread

asr-004295
04:07:23.800 --> 04:07:32.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: po ito, and then even before boarding ng aeroplano, kung sa tingin po ng sistema na hindi po siya

asr-004296
04:07:32.880 --> 04:07:39.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: dapat sumakay o pumasok ng Pilipinas, ibabato po yung information na po na yun in real time

asr-004297
04:07:39.640 --> 04:07:43.109
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: sa immigration officers po natin dito sa Pilipinas.

asr-004298
04:07:43.119 --> 04:07:45.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So, that would also...

asr-004299
04:07:46.000 --> 04:07:51.550
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: down to the benefit of the airlines, kasi hindi na po sila gagastos para pabalikin pa po ang isang tao

asr-004300
04:07:51.560 --> 04:07:54.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: na hindi naman po pa papasukin dito sa ating bansa.

asr-004301
04:07:54.439 --> 04:07:56.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So, yan po ang features po.

asr-004302
04:07:56.800 --> 04:08:03.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And then, Your Honor, we also have to take into account that the system being resorted to,

asr-004303
04:08:03.800 --> 04:08:13.710
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: or systems being resorted to, schemes, if I may call it that, resorted to by terrorists, criminals, are ever evolving.

asr-004304
04:08:13.720 --> 04:08:14.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So, itong sistema po na ito...

asr-004305
04:08:15.000 --> 04:08:23.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: aims to combat, or help, or be a tool to help our immigration officers in combating human trafficking,

asr-004306
04:08:23.960 --> 04:08:30.830
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: smuggling, drug and weapon smuggling, terrorism, money laundering, tax evasion, and organized crime.

asr-004307
04:08:30.840 --> 04:08:32.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yan po. Yan po yung sistema, Your Honor.

asr-004308
04:08:32.920 --> 04:08:36.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ano na-propose po yung Secure Reports Limited?

asr-004309
04:08:36.760 --> 04:08:38.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: That's correct, Your Honor. Secure Reports Limited.

asr-004310
04:08:38.319 --> 04:08:40.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sino pong mayari nito? Porin or Pilipino?

asr-004311
04:08:41.000 --> 04:08:45.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ano po? Ang Secure Report po is a company incorporated in the United States.

asr-004312
04:08:45.239 --> 04:08:50.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It's way back in 2000. Hindi po Philippine Corporation po yan.

asr-004313
04:08:50.520 --> 04:08:53.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They gave an unsolicited proposal.

asr-004314
04:08:53.159 --> 04:09:01.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Two years in the making na po, Your Honor, ang pag-review po ng iba't-iba ahensya ng gobyerno dito sa proposal po nila.

asr-004315
04:09:01.279 --> 04:09:10.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It went through the PPP Center, it went to the DOJ, it went through the Bureau of Immigration.

asr-004316
04:09:10.520 --> 04:09:12.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So, dalawang taon na po, Your Honor, na...

asr-004317
04:09:12.159 --> 04:09:14.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, but...

asr-004318
04:09:14.080 --> 04:09:15.309
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Do you mean that...

asr-004319
04:09:15.319 --> 04:09:20.590
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Your Honor, a sovereign company will have an access to the data of...

asr-004320
04:09:20.600 --> 04:09:27.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, a sovereign function at control po dito sa datos po na ito is retained by the Philippine government.

asr-004321
04:09:27.920 --> 04:09:31.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But how about the servers?

asr-004322
04:09:31.520 --> 04:09:33.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Tayo po may control dyan, Your Honor.

asr-004323
04:09:33.600 --> 04:09:37.710
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They only provide the tools and teach our people how to operate those.

asr-004324
04:09:37.720 --> 04:09:40.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But ultimately, ang control po...

asr-004325
04:09:40.199 --> 04:09:44.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Initially, they will be accessing these datas.

asr-004326
04:09:44.159 --> 04:09:45.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004327
04:09:45.239 --> 04:09:47.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They will help us provide...

asr-004328
04:09:47.279 --> 04:09:48.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They will help provide the tools...

asr-004329
04:09:48.159 --> 04:09:49.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Initially.

asr-004330
04:09:49.439 --> 04:09:52.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes or no?

asr-004331
04:09:52.199 --> 04:09:55.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As far as I know, Your Honor, no.

asr-004332
04:09:55.520 --> 04:09:58.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They will not have control over the data.

asr-004333
04:09:58.439 --> 04:09:59.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They will have no control...

asr-004334
04:09:59.239 --> 04:10:01.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: They will have no control over the data, Your Honor.

asr-004335
04:10:01.680 --> 04:10:01.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Okay.

asr-004336
04:10:02.000 --> 04:10:02.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Control is maintained by us.

asr-004337
04:10:02.880 --> 04:10:08.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Because I filed a resolution to investigate this particular contract.

asr-004338
04:10:08.439 --> 04:10:08.710
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004339
04:10:08.720 --> 04:10:09.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Aside from the...

asr-004340
04:10:09.520 --> 04:10:10.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004341
04:10:10.279 --> 04:10:11.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Aside from the...

asr-004342
04:10:11.840 --> 04:10:16.229
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kasi po, diba, yung tinanggal nga ng gobyerno, yung tinatanggal ngayon ng gobyerno, yung...

asr-004343
04:10:16.239 --> 04:10:16.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004344
04:10:16.520 --> 04:10:16.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004345
04:10:16.880 --> 04:10:29.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, parang ano, parang yung policy decision ng presidente ay tanggalan ng bawasan yung gastos ng mga pasahero.

asr-004346
04:10:29.840 --> 04:10:31.109
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pero ito dadagdagan.

asr-004347
04:10:31.119 --> 04:10:31.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Opo, Your Honor.

asr-004348
04:10:31.640 --> 04:10:34.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, ito po kasi, hindi po ito form ng tax, Your Honor.

asr-004349
04:10:34.600 --> 04:10:36.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ito po ay service fee.

asr-004350
04:10:36.600 --> 04:10:37.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So, hindi naman...

asr-004351
04:10:37.800 --> 04:10:39.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes, but that's the function of government.

asr-004352
04:10:39.640 --> 04:10:44.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: That's why we are collecting taxes, diba, from our people to provide services.

asr-004353
04:10:44.920 --> 04:10:46.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And that's...

asr-004354
04:10:46.640 --> 04:10:48.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Immigration service yan, yung...

asr-004355
04:10:48.640 --> 04:10:50.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor, we...

asr-004356
04:10:50.040 --> 04:10:51.229
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Cyber security.

asr-004357
04:10:51.239 --> 04:10:51.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, po.

asr-004358
04:10:51.439 --> 04:10:57.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, ang concern ko po dito, parang magkakontra yung policy.

asr-004359
04:10:57.640 --> 04:11:04.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: In fact, dito po sa travel tax, exempted na yung mga OFWs.

asr-004360
04:11:04.840 --> 04:11:07.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pero dito, kasama.

asr-004361
04:11:07.159 --> 04:11:14.349
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So, yung mga OFWs natin na nagdadala ng dolyar dito sa ating bansa, dadagdagan pa natin ng gastos.

asr-004362
04:11:14.359 --> 04:11:21.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Samantalang, yung revenue na nare-raise natin sa kanila, eh, pwede nating gastosin for this purpose.

asr-004363
04:11:21.560 --> 04:11:25.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We understand, Your Honor, and we fully agree po with your position.

asr-004364
04:11:25.159 --> 04:11:27.070
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As I've stated, this is a secure...

asr-004365
04:11:27.080 --> 04:11:27.469
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ano po?

asr-004366
04:11:27.479 --> 04:11:29.469
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Service fee po ito, Your Honor.

asr-004367
04:11:29.479 --> 04:11:37.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Meaning, hindi po namin pwede ipasa sa madlang bayan, taong bayan, sa ordinary taxpayer po, ang pag-gastos po dito.

asr-004368
04:11:37.040 --> 04:11:40.389
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang gagastos po dito ay ang mga taong nagka-travel.

asr-004369
04:11:40.399 --> 04:11:40.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi po lahat ng...

asr-004370
04:11:40.800 --> 04:11:42.389
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pag-Ws.

asr-004371
04:11:42.399 --> 04:11:44.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, admittedly po, sa kanila po, ang mga...

asr-004372
04:11:44.439 --> 04:11:46.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang mga pung-ticket, isasama po ang gastosin dito.

asr-004373
04:11:46.520 --> 04:11:47.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kaya nga, kaya nga.

asr-004374
04:11:47.840 --> 04:11:49.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, but if I may continue, Your Honor.

asr-004375
04:11:49.640 --> 04:11:55.550
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, ang gastosin po pagdating sa ticket, hindi po sinasagot po yan ng OFWs.

asr-004376
04:11:55.560 --> 04:11:57.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Sagot po yan ng mga employers nila.

asr-004377
04:11:57.680 --> 04:12:04.109
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang employers po, under an executive order, and under various agreements with other countries,

asr-004378
04:12:04.119 --> 04:12:11.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: ang sumasagot po yan ng gastosin po sa pamasahe, at including na po, kung sakali ma-approvean po ito,

asr-004379
04:12:11.920 --> 04:12:14.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: yung service fee po na ito, ay sasagotin ng...

asr-004380
04:12:14.319 --> 04:12:22.070
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: So hindi OFWs po natin ang sasagot.

asr-004381
04:12:22.080 --> 04:12:25.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ito po yung mga kumpanyang kukuha po sa kanila ang sasagot dito.

asr-004382
04:12:25.319 --> 04:12:31.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And if I may, Your Honor, ito pong sistema po na ito, ginagamit na po yan worldwide.

asr-004383
04:12:31.040 --> 04:12:37.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi lang po natin siguro napapansin, pero ang ibang bansa po, nilalagay po yan, nakasama ng gastosin sa mga ticket po.

asr-004384
04:12:37.239 --> 04:12:42.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: As I've stated earlier, Your Honor, ang Australia po, charges about 2,600...

asr-004385
04:12:42.960 --> 04:12:44.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sir, you said Hong Kong is doing this.

asr-004386
04:12:44.439 --> 04:12:45.750
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004387
04:12:45.760 --> 04:12:51.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: I've been traveling to Hong Kong for quite some time, pero wala akong nakikita ng gano'n.

asr-004388
04:12:51.199 --> 04:12:54.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Baka po sa breakdown, makikita po natin, Your Honor.

asr-004389
04:12:54.600 --> 04:13:05.030
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yan po, Hong Kong charges 1,800, Japan charges 1,200, Singapore charges 2,400, Australia charges 2,600.

asr-004390
04:13:05.040 --> 04:13:10.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We charge 240 pesos. So ganyan po yung comparison po, Your Honor.

asr-004391
04:13:10.640 --> 04:13:15.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: The total project cost is 10,740,000.

asr-004392
04:13:15.479 --> 04:13:19.389
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, for the first five years po yan, 10.7 billion, Your Honor.

asr-004393
04:13:19.399 --> 04:13:26.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But ang security report po promised a technology maintenance upgrade po.

asr-004394
04:13:26.279 --> 04:13:33.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Upgrade not only of the systems, but also of the training for people every four years over the 20-year period.

asr-004395
04:13:33.640 --> 04:13:34.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kasama po dito sa 10 billion?

asr-004396
04:13:34.720 --> 04:13:35.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi po, Your Honor.

asr-004397
04:13:35.680 --> 04:13:37.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So another increase?

asr-004398
04:13:37.159 --> 04:13:38.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi po, Your Honor.

asr-004399
04:13:38.439 --> 04:13:44.750
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang commitment po nila is during the lifetime of the...

asr-004400
04:13:44.760 --> 04:13:51.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The agreement sa 20 years po na yan, ganyan lang po naka napag-usapan po namin na charges nila.

asr-004401
04:13:51.199 --> 04:13:53.389
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ano po ang capex nila for the whole project?

asr-004402
04:13:53.399 --> 04:14:02.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: For the whole project po, over the 20-year period, so 10.7 initially, additional, I think, 52.5 billion over the 20-year period po.

asr-004403
04:14:02.880 --> 04:14:03.590
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So 62 point...

asr-004404
04:14:03.600 --> 04:14:07.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: It is in the proposed contract?

asr-004405
04:14:07.479 --> 04:14:14.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It is. Everything is under the proposed contract and under review by all pertinent government agencies.

asr-004406
04:14:14.239 --> 04:14:21.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: The total estimated collection is about 202 billion.

asr-004407
04:14:21.199 --> 04:14:22.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Probably, Your Honor.

asr-004408
04:14:22.439 --> 04:14:25.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And the share of the private corporation is 192 billion.

asr-004409
04:14:25.960 --> 04:14:34.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Ang breakdown po, if I may, Your Honor, is per kada apat na dolyar po, 380 goes to the proponent, 20 cents goes to the Philippine government.

asr-004410
04:14:34.920 --> 04:14:35.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 5%.

asr-004411
04:14:35.479 --> 04:14:38.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 5% share.

asr-004412
04:14:38.199 --> 04:14:38.870
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004413
04:14:38.880 --> 04:14:40.670
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So this is about 10 billion.

asr-004414
04:14:40.680 --> 04:14:41.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Tama po, 5%.

asr-004415
04:14:41.279 --> 04:14:44.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 95% of the collections will go to the private.

asr-004416
04:14:44.279 --> 04:14:45.710
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: A provider.

asr-004417
04:14:45.720 --> 04:14:46.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004418
04:14:46.439 --> 04:14:49.229
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And only 5%.

asr-004419
04:14:49.239 --> 04:14:50.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: To the government.

asr-004420
04:14:50.279 --> 04:14:54.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sir, why are you still giving this to the government?

asr-004421
04:14:54.040 --> 04:14:54.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Sorry, sir.

asr-004422
04:14:54.239 --> 04:14:55.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Sorry, Your Honor.

asr-004423
04:14:55.199 --> 04:14:57.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: This is your service, immigration, to our people.

asr-004424
04:14:57.560 --> 04:14:58.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Why are you still giving this to the government?

asr-004425
04:14:58.840 --> 04:15:04.349
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It will fund the projects of the Bureau of Immigration.

asr-004426
04:15:04.359 --> 04:15:06.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: And yes, sir.

asr-004427
04:15:06.680 --> 04:15:10.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Immigration, projects of immigration for this?

asr-004428
04:15:10.560 --> 04:15:13.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Will also return to the benefit of the government, Your Honor.

asr-004429
04:15:13.800 --> 04:15:19.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Why would you fund another project out of this particular project?

asr-004430
04:15:19.479 --> 04:15:22.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But this will go to the National Treasury, Your Honor.

asr-004431
04:15:22.640 --> 04:15:23.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: That's it.

asr-004432
04:15:23.439 --> 04:15:27.309
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And then, since we are the agency...

asr-004433
04:15:27.319 --> 04:15:30.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So this is still a business of the government?

asr-004434
04:15:30.159 --> 04:15:32.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: There's a profit.

asr-004435
04:15:32.279 --> 04:15:35.750
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The service is what the business does.

asr-004436
04:15:35.760 --> 04:15:36.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: No, Your Honor.

asr-004437
04:15:37.000 --> 04:15:38.149
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We are charging...

asr-004438
04:15:38.159 --> 04:15:40.309
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: It's 5% profit.

asr-004439
04:15:40.319 --> 04:15:41.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It's not...

asr-004440
04:15:41.800 --> 04:15:43.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: It's the share between...

asr-004441
04:15:43.439 --> 04:15:46.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Private proponent and the government, Your Honor.

asr-004442
04:15:46.199 --> 04:15:49.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Is this a part of the Swiss Challenge?

asr-004443
04:15:49.199 --> 04:15:50.309
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004444
04:15:50.319 --> 04:15:53.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: There was a comparative challenge, which is the Swiss Challenge, which...

asr-004445
04:15:53.600 --> 04:15:58.229
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Who gave the comparative challenge?

asr-004446
04:15:58.239 --> 04:16:00.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We sent out notices, Your Honor.

asr-004447
04:16:01.000 --> 04:16:02.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: But no one came?

asr-004448
04:16:02.040 --> 04:16:03.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: No one challenged, Your Honor.

asr-004449
04:16:03.800 --> 04:16:05.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Usually, that's the case.

asr-004450
04:16:05.479 --> 04:16:06.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Usually, that's the case.

asr-004451
04:16:06.520 --> 04:16:13.389
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Anyway, can we give a copy before the plenary of the proposed contract?

asr-004452
04:16:13.399 --> 04:16:13.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004453
04:16:13.640 --> 04:16:31.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And the terms of reference and the proposal of the company and the resolution of your PBAC, the bidding committee.

asr-004454
04:16:31.080 --> 04:16:31.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004455
04:16:31.680 --> 04:16:34.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: We will provide all the necessary documents to you.

asr-004456
04:16:34.920 --> 04:16:36.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Before the plenary?

asr-004457
04:16:37.000 --> 04:16:37.550
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004458
04:16:37.560 --> 04:16:42.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: From the PPP, DOJ, Bureau of Immigration.

asr-004459
04:16:42.279 --> 04:16:42.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: All of that.

asr-004460
04:16:43.000 --> 04:16:47.950
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, we will provide it to you as requested, Your Honor.

asr-004461
04:16:47.960 --> 04:16:50.710
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Another topic.

asr-004462
04:16:50.720 --> 04:16:51.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Last question.

asr-004463
04:16:51.560 --> 04:16:52.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: My last question.

asr-004464
04:16:52.479 --> 04:16:53.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Thank you.

asr-004465
04:16:53.960 --> 04:16:55.389
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Still on immigration.

asr-004466
04:16:55.399 --> 04:16:55.670
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004467
04:16:55.680 --> 04:16:57.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: There are a lot of issues with you.

asr-004468
04:16:57.479 --> 04:16:59.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Joseph C. has been in jail for a year.

asr-004469
04:16:59.920 --> 04:17:01.189
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004470
04:17:01.199 --> 04:17:03.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: What is the case of Joseph C.?

asr-004471
04:17:03.199 --> 04:17:08.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Joseph C., Your Honor, is a fake Filipino, Your Honor.

asr-004472
04:17:08.600 --> 04:17:09.349
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes.

asr-004473
04:17:09.359 --> 04:17:12.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe around 100,000 here in the Philippines.

asr-004474
04:17:12.080 --> 04:17:14.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004475
04:17:14.239 --> 04:17:15.109
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe around 100,000 here in the Philippines.

asr-004476
04:17:15.119 --> 04:17:15.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 100,000.

asr-004477
04:17:15.840 --> 04:17:20.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: If you arrest all the big businessmen, our economy will collapse.

asr-004478
04:17:21.000 --> 04:17:31.429
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, based on intelligence information that we gathered, Joseph C. is attending the communist party meetings in China.

asr-004479
04:17:31.439 --> 04:17:38.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Well, I asked during the budget hearing last year, I asked Secretary Año kung spy si Joseph C.

asr-004480
04:17:38.080 --> 04:17:43.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sabi niya sa akin, negosyante lang 'yan. Wala kaming information.

asr-004481
04:17:43.640 --> 04:17:46.469
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, ang pinaglalaban din po namin...

asr-004482
04:17:46.479 --> 04:17:48.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: What is your basis for saying that?

asr-004483
04:17:48.760 --> 04:17:52.469
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Your Honor, intelligence information from government agencies.

asr-004484
04:17:52.479 --> 04:17:52.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: From?

asr-004485
04:17:52.920 --> 04:17:53.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: From what government agency?

asr-004486
04:17:53.560 --> 04:17:54.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: From?

asr-004487
04:17:54.920 --> 04:17:55.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: What government agency?

asr-004488
04:17:56.000 --> 04:17:59.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Because I talked to Secretary Año, tinanong ko.

asr-004489
04:17:59.199 --> 04:18:00.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kilala ko kasi, matagal na si...

asr-004490
04:18:00.800 --> 04:18:03.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Siguro mga 15 years ko nang kilala si Joseph C.

asr-004491
04:18:03.560 --> 04:18:04.269
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004492
04:18:04.279 --> 04:18:07.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So kilala ko naman na negosyante.

asr-004493
04:18:07.159 --> 04:18:12.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Nagbabayad naman ng buwis dito sa Pilipinas.

asr-004494
04:18:12.960 --> 04:18:17.750
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: The information I can relate to you after this meeting, Your Honor.

asr-004495
04:18:17.760 --> 04:18:19.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: What agency?

asr-004496
04:18:19.439 --> 04:18:21.910
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: I can relate it to you, Your Honor.

asr-004497
04:18:21.920 --> 04:18:25.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alam ko lang na agency na nagtatanong diyan, Senate, eh.

asr-004498
04:18:25.159 --> 04:18:28.229
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Hindi po, Your Honor. Hindi po Senate.

asr-004499
04:18:28.239 --> 04:18:33.790
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: But ang amin naman pong, Your Honor, pinaglalaban din pagdating naman po sa fake Filipinos

asr-004500
04:18:33.800 --> 04:18:42.990
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: is 'yung sistema natin ng pag-issue ng mga documents na pinanghahawakan po natin bilang Pilipino,

asr-004501
04:18:43.000 --> 04:18:48.630
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: like 'yung pasaporte, 'yung mga birth certificates na nababayaran na po, Your Honor.

asr-004502
04:18:48.640 --> 04:18:54.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alam niyo po, I've been talking to the Filipino-Chinese Chamber of Commerce, the officers.

asr-004503
04:18:55.000 --> 04:19:00.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: In fact, I filed a proposal to amend the immigration law.

asr-004504
04:19:00.080 --> 04:19:07.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kasi po mahigit, baka 200,000 'yung mga illegal aliens dito,

asr-004505
04:19:07.520 --> 04:19:09.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: pero mostly Chinese.

asr-004506
04:19:09.080 --> 04:19:12.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Pumapasok po sila dito using fake documents,

asr-004507
04:19:12.439 --> 04:19:14.229
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: marriage certificates, birth certificates.

asr-004508
04:19:14.239 --> 04:19:16.870
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: So nagpo-provide din 'yung mga agencies natin.

asr-004509
04:19:16.880 --> 04:19:17.590
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004510
04:19:17.600 --> 04:19:20.870
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: They facilitate for certain fees.

asr-004511
04:19:20.880 --> 04:19:25.469
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At ang gusto nila talaga, kung at least mga seven, ten years na sila dito,

asr-004512
04:19:25.479 --> 04:19:29.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: wala naman silang criminal record, wala naman silang...

asr-004513
04:19:29.040 --> 04:19:31.590
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: and they're willing to pay ten million.

asr-004514
04:19:31.600 --> 04:19:32.389
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, sir.

asr-004515
04:19:32.399 --> 04:19:36.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: And that will amount to billions of revenue,

asr-004516
04:19:36.840 --> 04:19:42.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: kaysa daw po tuwing Pasko, dinadaanan sila ng mga immigration agents diyan sa Binondo

asr-004517
04:19:42.640 --> 04:19:44.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: at hinihingan sila.

asr-004518
04:19:44.760 --> 04:19:50.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Eh mag-one-time legitimize na nila 'yung kanilang status.

asr-004519
04:19:51.000 --> 04:19:57.030
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alam niyo, ang masama dito, may pinag-interesan 'yung property nung isang Chinese,

asr-004520
04:19:57.040 --> 04:19:59.109
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: o, huhulihin.

asr-004521
04:19:59.119 --> 04:20:00.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 'Di ba? Ganoon ang mangyayari.

asr-004522
04:20:01.000 --> 04:20:04.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Ganoon ang mangyayari.

asr-004523
04:20:04.159 --> 04:20:06.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bakit hindi natin i-legitimize?

asr-004524
04:20:06.279 --> 04:20:11.070
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: 'Yung ngang ibang mga Chinese, 'yung mga taipans dito, mga tycoons,

asr-004525
04:20:11.080 --> 04:20:12.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: they are more Filipino than

asr-004526
04:20:12.920 --> 04:20:14.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: many of us

asr-004527
04:20:14.800 --> 04:20:19.189
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: in terms of contributing to the national economy.

asr-004528
04:20:19.199 --> 04:20:20.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Bakit hindi natin ayusin ito?

asr-004529
04:20:20.640 --> 04:20:21.510
BI Commissioner Joel Anthony M. Viado: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-004530
04:20:21.520 --> 04:20:23.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe Secretary Bida can...

asr-004531
04:20:23.920 --> 04:20:26.269
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes.

asr-004532
04:20:26.279 --> 04:20:27.309
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes.

asr-004533
04:20:27.319 --> 04:20:32.149
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Actually, we have a pending for the amendment of the Immigration Act.

asr-004534
04:20:32.159 --> 04:20:36.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So that their additional powers can enter here.

asr-004535
04:20:36.439 --> 04:20:37.830
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Additional powers to address this.

asr-004536
04:20:37.840 --> 04:20:42.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: It also reached us that we have one...

asr-004537
04:20:42.439 --> 04:20:51.109
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: It also reached us that we have one municipality that manufactures birth certificates, right?

asr-004538
04:20:51.119 --> 04:20:51.550
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes.

asr-004539
04:20:51.560 --> 04:20:52.109
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: In Mineralo.

asr-004540
04:20:52.119 --> 04:20:52.830
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes.

asr-004541
04:20:52.840 --> 04:20:56.070
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: These are the things that, when we see it,

asr-004542
04:20:56.080 --> 04:20:59.269
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: for moving forward, I completely agree with you,

asr-004543
04:20:59.279 --> 04:21:08.389
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: so that there won't be opportunities for enterprising so-called public servants.

asr-004544
04:21:08.399 --> 04:21:09.750
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes.

asr-004545
04:21:09.760 --> 04:21:12.510
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Because we should send a message that...

asr-004546
04:21:12.520 --> 04:21:17.990
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: that there should be a cut-clear criteria for us to look at this,

asr-004547
04:21:18.000 --> 04:21:19.710
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: whether you're qualified or not.

asr-004548
04:21:19.720 --> 04:21:21.109
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Then, you enter here.

asr-004549
04:21:21.119 --> 04:21:23.750
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: When you enter, then we're able.

asr-004550
04:21:23.760 --> 04:21:27.990
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Of course, a consequential benefit would be collection of the proper fees.

asr-004551
04:21:28.000 --> 04:21:30.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Alam niyo, sa Caloocan, motorcycle...

asr-004552
04:21:30.560 --> 04:21:36.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Sa district ko po, Grace Park, Motorcycle Capital of Luzon.

asr-004553
04:21:36.279 --> 04:21:40.830
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At karamihan po ng mga Chinese businessman doon, 'yung mga maliliit na businessman,

asr-004554
04:21:40.840 --> 04:21:42.790
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: nagtitinda ng motor parts.

asr-004555
04:21:42.800 --> 04:21:48.149
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Matagal na po sila diyan, pero talagang illegal po 'yung entry nila.

asr-004556
04:21:48.159 --> 04:21:51.550
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Mga fake documents.

asr-004557
04:21:51.560 --> 04:21:55.510
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At dahil po dito sa nangyayaring ito, marami pong umaalis, eh.

asr-004558
04:21:55.520 --> 04:21:55.910
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Umaalis na.

asr-004559
04:21:55.920 --> 04:22:00.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: May mga asawa po 'yan na Pilipina

asr-004560
04:22:00.760 --> 04:22:03.109
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: na minsan naiiwan na nila.

asr-004561
04:22:03.119 --> 04:22:09.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At kung aalis po lahat 'yung mga illegals doon sa lugar namin,

asr-004562
04:22:09.640 --> 04:22:12.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: babagsak talaga 'yung ekonomiya ng lugar namin.

asr-004563
04:22:12.279 --> 04:22:18.990
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Kaya nga po siguro, kung ayos naman, may NBI clearance,

asr-004564
04:22:19.000 --> 04:22:21.750
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: mayroong national security clearance,

asr-004565
04:22:21.760 --> 04:22:23.950
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: wala naman pong mga kaso,

asr-004566
04:22:23.960 --> 04:22:26.109
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: at matagal na sila dito,

asr-004567
04:22:26.119 --> 04:22:29.870
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: eh baka puwede na nating i-legitimize 'yung kanilang stay.

asr-004568
04:22:29.880 --> 04:22:33.670
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Katulad din naman 'yan ng mga Pilipino sa America,

asr-004569
04:22:33.680 --> 04:22:37.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: mga TNT na nale-legitimize.

asr-004570
04:22:37.439 --> 04:22:42.269
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: At hindi naman natin gawin 'yan dito sa mga kapitbahay natin,

asr-004571
04:22:42.279 --> 04:22:45.309
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: na Filipino-Chinese.

asr-004572
04:22:45.319 --> 04:22:47.429
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Maybe the DOJ can work on that.

asr-004573
04:22:47.439 --> 04:22:49.750
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: With your permission, Your Honor,

asr-004574
04:22:49.760 --> 04:22:53.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: we will properly come up with a roadmap on this.

asr-004575
04:22:53.439 --> 04:22:55.790
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Because so that it won't go back and forth.

asr-004576
04:22:55.800 --> 04:22:58.750
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Because just like what I've mentioned,

asr-004577
04:22:58.760 --> 04:22:59.910
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: we don't want to...

asr-004578
04:22:59.920 --> 04:23:01.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Because we have a lot of work to do.

asr-004579
04:23:01.439 --> 04:23:03.349
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: I want it to be over.

asr-004580
04:23:03.359 --> 04:23:05.469
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So that this problem will be over.

asr-004581
04:23:05.479 --> 04:23:08.070
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: With your permission, with permission of everyone,

asr-004582
04:23:08.080 --> 04:23:10.870
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: we will duly consult you.

asr-004583
04:23:10.880 --> 04:23:11.950
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Of course, we need your...

asr-004584
04:23:11.960 --> 04:23:14.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: We need your learnings on the ground.

asr-004585
04:23:14.439 --> 04:23:15.590
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: We need your know-how.

asr-004586
04:23:15.600 --> 04:23:18.429
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: You need to be more aware of the movements of those...

asr-004587
04:23:18.439 --> 04:23:20.309
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: You said it, right?

asr-004588
04:23:20.319 --> 04:23:21.710
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Those who have become friends.

asr-004589
04:23:21.720 --> 04:23:24.790
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: We're happy with the development of our economy.

asr-004590
04:23:24.800 --> 04:23:27.070
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So I'll be tasking...

asr-004591
04:23:27.080 --> 04:23:28.630
Rep. Edgar R. Erice: Yes. Thank you.

asr-004592
04:23:28.640 --> 04:23:29.990
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Together with the BI,

asr-004593
04:23:30.000 --> 04:23:32.830
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: once and for all, of course,

asr-004594
04:23:32.840 --> 04:23:34.510
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: we need the former commissioner,

asr-004595
04:23:34.520 --> 04:23:35.630
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: the wisdom of the former commissioner.

asr-004596
04:23:35.640 --> 04:23:36.630
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: I consulted also...

asr-004597
04:23:36.640 --> 04:23:38.990
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So that we can see.

asr-004598
04:23:39.000 --> 04:23:41.710
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: So that it won't go back and forth.

asr-004601
04:23:41.720 --> 04:23:45.630
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: And we can raise a lot of revenue

asr-004602
04:23:45.640 --> 04:23:48.830
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: from these people.

asr-004603
04:23:48.840 --> 04:23:49.910
DOJ Secretary Fredderick A. Vida: Yes. Everything, Your Honor,

asr-004604
