Rep. Allan U. Ty: proposed budget,

asr-005664
05:01:43.600 --> 05:01:46.678
Rep. Allan U. Ty: how much is under special account?

asr-005665
05:01:46.678 --> 05:01:51.376
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: What budget?

asr-005666
05:01:51.436 --> 05:02:01.810
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, it's $1.8 billion.

asr-005667
05:02:03.329 --> 05:02:05.328
Rep. Allan U. Ty: $1.780 billion?

asr-005668
05:02:05.328 --> 05:02:06.468
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-005669
05:02:06.468 --> 05:02:09.946
Rep. Allan U. Ty: What is the source of your special account in the general fund, Mr. Administrator?

asr-005670
05:02:09.946 --> 05:02:14.543
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the special account is Fund 151.

asr-005671
05:02:14.543 --> 05:02:20.060
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: It is a special account provided by PD 1529,

asr-005672
05:02:20.060 --> 05:02:26.836
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: where, from our collections, we are allowed to retain 20% of our earnings, Paul.

asr-005673
05:02:26.836 --> 05:02:27.776
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor.

asr-005674
05:02:28.116 --> 05:02:29.095
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Please settle down.

asr-005675
05:02:32.503 --> 05:02:33.143
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Quiet, please.

asr-005676
05:02:36.141 --> 05:02:38.480
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Where does the 80% of the collection go?

asr-005677
05:02:38.700 --> 05:02:40.699
Rep. Allan U. Ty: How about the balance of 80%?

asr-005678
05:02:40.819 --> 05:02:41.518
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Where does it go?

asr-005679
05:02:41.518 --> 05:02:45.256
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the 80% goes directly to the National Treasury,

asr-005680
05:02:45.656 --> 05:02:52.392
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: and we retain 20% subject to the approval of the DBM on the releases of the 20%.

asr-005681
05:02:52.392 --> 05:02:57.210
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So the 20% in the amount of 1.7,

asr-005682
05:02:57.830 --> 05:03:00.308
Rep. Allan U. Ty: can we use that amount?

asr-005683
05:03:00.308 --> 05:03:06.185
Rep. Allan U. Ty: To pay for titling of free patents issued by the DENR?

asr-005684
05:03:06.185 --> 05:03:18.978
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, the 1.7 billion is 15% only out of the 20% it represents.

asr-005685
05:03:18.978 --> 05:03:52.240
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, we believe that it can be used for it.

asr-005686
05:03:52.240 --> 05:03:57.717
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: The coverage of the special account refers to MOOE accounts and capital outlay.

asr-005687
05:03:58.436 --> 05:04:06.672
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Because, Administrator, there are thousands of unclaimed free patents before the Registry of Deeds all over the Philippines.

asr-005688
05:04:06.672 --> 05:04:15.707
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So, probably, can you account for the free patents, unclaimed free patents, in all the Registry of Deeds all over the Philippines?

asr-005689
05:04:15.707 --> 05:04:17.106
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor, you are correct.

asr-005690
05:04:17.106 --> 05:04:21.724
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have made that observation in our visits to the different Registers of Deeds.

asr-005691
05:04:21.724 --> 05:04:27.860
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: We have observed several, if not thousands, of unregistered patents previously.

asr-005692
05:04:27.860 --> 05:04:38.615
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: This was covered by an agreement with the DENR, which paid for the registration of the patents.

asr-005693
05:04:38.615 --> 05:04:42.612
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Subsequently, they removed that funding.

asr-005694
05:04:42.612 --> 05:04:54.966
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: So, perhaps with the approval of the DBM, we can utilize it in registering some of these, or all the remaining patents issued.

asr-005695
05:04:54.966 --> 05:04:57.684
Rep. Allan U. Ty: To be taken from the special account?

asr-005696
05:04:57.844 --> 05:05:02.581
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor, if we can maximize the utilization to 20%.

asr-005697
05:05:02.581 --> 05:05:03.661
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Thank you.

asr-005698
05:05:03.661 --> 05:05:09.678
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So, on the other matter, Mr. Administrator, what is the legal responsibility of the

asr-005699
05:05:09.678 --> 05:05:15.714
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Registry of Deeds and the LRA for the safekeeping maintenance of Certificate of Titles?

asr-005700
05:05:15.714 --> 05:05:16.614
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Please, quiet down.

asr-005701
05:05:16.614 --> 05:05:32.685
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honour, under PD 1529, the function of the main function of the Registers of Deeds is the main repository of all the

asr-005702
05:05:32.725 --> 05:05:34.584
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: titles and supporting documents.

asr-005703
05:05:34.844 --> 05:05:36.343
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So it's a registry of deeds?

asr-005704
05:05:36.523 --> 05:05:37.063
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Yes, Your Honor.

asr-005705
05:05:37.502 --> 05:05:44.639
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Is the registry of deeds required to prepare an inventory of titles which have been lost,

asr-005706
05:05:44.958 --> 05:05:48.436
Rep. Allan U. Ty: destroyed, or rendered unusable by deterioration?

asr-005707
05:05:48.436 --> 05:05:56.372
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, under PD 1529, the RDs are obliged to conduct an inventory annually.

asr-005708
05:05:56.372 --> 05:06:03.748
Rep. Allan U. Ty: I would suppose that would also include all titles, whether it has been lost or damaged in their custody.

asr-005709
05:06:05.227 --> 05:06:13.763
Rep. Allan U. Ty: In case of lost administrator of title, who has the legal responsibility for judicial reconstitution?

asr-005710
05:06:14.322 --> 05:06:19.420
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Your Honor, unfortunately, when the title is lost, the RD copy is lost.

asr-005711
05:06:19.420 --> 05:06:25.176
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under RA 26, as amended by RA 6732,

asr-005712
05:06:25.176 --> 05:06:30.054
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: the responsibility is given to the owner of the title.

asr-005713
05:06:30.633 --> 05:06:34.431
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: The responsibility was taken away from the RD.

asr-005714
05:06:34.871 --> 05:06:39.609
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Previously, the RD was allowed to initiate reconstitution cases,

asr-005715
05:06:39.828 --> 05:06:48.164
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: but because of the passage of the law and because of a Supreme Court decision involving the RD of Malabon or Mandaluyong,

asr-005716
05:06:48.164 --> 05:06:54.161
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: the Supreme Court said that the RDs cannot undertake the filing.

asr-005717
05:06:55.160 --> 05:06:56.319
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under the reconstitution case.

asr-005718
05:06:57.679 --> 05:07:03.376
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Sir Administrator, is there no exception to the rule under RA 6732?

asr-005719
05:07:03.695 --> 05:07:08.553
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Under RA 26, as amended by RA 6732,

asr-005720
05:07:09.772 --> 05:07:14.050
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: administrative reconstitution can be undertaken by the LRA

asr-005721
05:07:14.330 --> 05:07:24.884
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: if the Administrator has evaluated that at least 10% of the titles in the RD has been lost,

asr-005722
05:07:25.144 --> 05:07:29.741
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: But in no case should it be less than 500 titles.

asr-005723
05:07:30.601 --> 05:07:40.895
Rep. Allan U. Ty: As you mentioned earlier, Mr. Administrator, you said the Registry of Deeds are required or mandated to have an inventory of lost titles.

asr-005724
05:07:41.355 --> 05:07:46.652
Rep. Allan U. Ty: So based on the submission, did the Registry of Deeds make the submission?

asr-005725
05:07:47.392 --> 05:07:51.030
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: They are required to conduct an inventory which should also include all lost titles.

asr-005726
05:07:51.030 --> 05:07:59.805
LRA Administrator Gerardo P. Sirios: Some of the RDs have complied with the provisions of the law, and we are closely monitoring also the other RDs, Your Honor.

asr-005727
05:08:00.245 --> 05:08:18.295
Rep. Allan U. Ty: Let's say in case the administrative threshold is not met, what can your office do to assist those lost titles, individual lost titles,

asr-005728
05:08:18.295 --> 05:08:20.054
Rep. Allan U. Ty: considering that the loss?

